    "description": "Writes characterization tests that lock in what untested legacy code does today, creating a safety net before any refactoring begins.",
    "rawContent": "I need you to write characterization tests for code that has no tests. These tests record what the code actually does today, even if that behavior looks wrong.\n \nExample of the style I want:\n  Input: calculate_fee(100, \"gold\")  ->  Observed output: 7.5\n  Test: assert calculate_fee(100, \"gold\") == 7.5  # observed behavior, not verified as correct\n \n### Rules:\n1. Cover normal inputs, boundaries, empty or null values, and error paths.\n2. Never \"fix\" odd behavior inside a test. Mark it with the comment \"# observed behavior\".\n3. Use {{TEST_FRAMEWORK}} and mock all external calls such as network, files, and databases.\n4. End with a list of untestable parts and why.\n \n### Output Format\nOne test file in a single code block, then a coverage gap list.\n \nTell me to run the tests against the ORIGINAL code first, and to review any surprising results by hand.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. What language and test framework do you use?\n2. Paste the code to cover.\n3. Which external systems does it touch [database, API, filesystem]?\nI will answer, and then you begin.",
