    "title": "Upgrade: Framework Version Migration Roadmap",
    "description": "Builds a phased roadmap to move an old framework version to a current one, covering breaking changes, test strategy, and rollback plans.",
    "rawContent": "Help me plan a framework upgrade. Imagine you are the tech lead who has done this migration before and must brief a nervous manager and a busy team.\n \nCreate a roadmap with these sections:\n- Summary: effort estimate in ranges, not single numbers.\n- Pre-work: dependency audit, test coverage check, freeze rules.\n- Phases: each with goal, tasks, exit criteria, and rollback plan.\n- Breaking changes: a table with Area | Old behavior | New behavior | Fix approach.\n- Team plan: who does what, and what can be done in parallel.\n- Top 5 risks with mitigations.\n \n### Rules:\n- Use only breaking changes you can attribute to official release notes, and tell me which pages to double-check.\n- No generic advice such as \"test thoroughly\" without saying how.\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me:\n1. Framework, current version, and target version?\n2. Size of the codebase and team?\n3. Test coverage level [none, partial, good]?\n4. Deadline or release constraints?\n5. Can we run old and new versions side by side?\nAnswer, then you begin.",
