    "description": "Writes a clear pull request title, description, and reviewer checklist for a refactoring change so reviewers can approve with confidence.",
    "rawContent": "Write a pull request description for my refactoring. Reviewers are busy, so keep it scannable.\n \nFormat exactly like this:\nTitle: (under 70 characters, starts with a verb)\nSummary: 2 sentences\nWhy now: 1-2 sentences\nWhat changed: bullets, grouped by file or module\nWhat did NOT change: bullets, to reassure reviewers\nHow I verified: test commands and results\nReviewer checklist: 5 checkbox items\nRollback: one sentence\n \n### Do NOT:\n- Use buzzwords like \"streamline\" or \"leverage\"\n- Claim tests passed unless I tell you so\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste the diff or describe the changes.\n2. Which tests did you run and what happened?\n3. Are there any risky areas you want reviewers to focus on?\nThen write the PR text.",
