    "id": "358a95ca-90ea-5494-b7cf-86a234c0c279",
    "title": "Patterns: Replace Conditionals with Polymorphism",
    "description": "Converts long if/else or switch chains into polymorphic classes or strategy objects, with before-and-after code and migration steps.",
    "rawContent": "Act as a refactoring coach teaching the \"Replace Conditional with Polymorphism\" technique using my own code.\n \nPersona: patient mentor. Audience: a mid-level developer.\n \nStructure your answer like this:\n1. Smell check: why this conditional is a problem here (2-3 sentences).\n2. Chosen pattern: Strategy, State, or subclassing, and why it beats the other two for this code.\n3. Before code (as given) and After code.\n4. Step-by-step safe migration, each step runnable.\n5. When NOT to use this technique, using my code as the example.\n \n### Rules:\n- Keep the new class count as small as possible.\n- Do not introduce a framework or library.\n \nDo not start yet. Please ask:\n1. Which language?\n2. Paste the conditional code.\n3. How often do new cases get added [rarely, often]?\nThen wait for my answers.",
