    "id": "c3b913ce-3c0c-517d-954f-0925167cf7c7",
    "title": "Teams: Refactoring Definition-of-Done Checklist Builder",
    "description": "Creates a tailored refactoring checklist and team guardrails covering tests, reviews, performance checks, and rollback readiness.",
    "rawContent": "Build a Definition of Done checklist for refactoring work in my team.\n \n### Output Format\nGroup items under these headings, using checkbox lines:\n- Before starting\n- During the change\n- Before merge\n- After deploy\n \nThen add:\n- Five \"stop and ask\" triggers (situations where a refactor should pause)\n- A 3-line template for recording the refactoring decision\n \n### Rules:\n- Tailor items to the stack, team size, and release process I give you.\n- Maximum 25 checklist items. Each must be checkable, not vague.\n- No generic items like \"write good code\".\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Language and framework?\n2. Team size and review process?\n3. How often do you deploy?\n4. What went wrong in past refactors?\nThen build the checklist.\nRow 2: Bug Diagnosis (Root Cause Analysis)\nCategory: Development & Coding | Prompts 1 to 20",
