    "id": "ef0939ce-ec21-5c24-89bc-a9ce6dbb87f2",
    "title": "Boundaries: Domain-Driven Design Service Splitter",
    "description": "Applies domain-driven design to find bounded contexts in your business domain and map them to service boundaries.",
    "rawContent": "Run a short event-storming session with me, then convert the result into service boundaries.\n \nPhase 1 - Ask me for business events in past tense (for example \"Order Placed\").\nPhase 2 - Group events into aggregates and bounded contexts.\nPhase 3 - Show the contexts in a table: Context | Aggregates | Key events | Owner team | Upstream/Downstream.\nPhase 4 - Flag places where one concept has two meanings (for example \"Customer\" in billing versus support) and propose a translation layer.\nPhase 5 - Recommend which contexts become services first.\n \n### Rules:\n- Use the vocabulary of my business, not generic tech names.\n- If two contexts change together every release, say they probably belong together.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe your business in a few sentences.\n2. List the main things that happen in it (any order, rough is fine).\nThen we begin Phase 1.",
