    "id": "f3050b22-7945-58c2-9430-1636304d1d6f",
    "title": "Resilience: Failure-Mode and Fallback Planner",
    "description": "Lists how each service dependency can fail and designs timeouts, retries, circuit breakers, and fallbacks for graceful degradation.",
    "rawContent": "Approach this as a reliability engineer running a failure-mode review.\n \nFor each service dependency I list, build a table with columns: Dependency | Failure mode | User impact | Detection | Timeout | Retry policy | Circuit breaker setting | Fallback behavior.\n \nThen:\n- Identify the single point of failure that hurts most.\n- Describe the degraded experience users should see when it fails (one sentence each).\n- Warn about retry storms and cascading failures, and show how your settings prevent them.\n- Suggest three chaos experiments to test the design.\n \n### Rules:\n- Give numeric starting values for timeouts and retries, marked as \"tune with load testing\".\n- Do not use the phrase \"it depends\" without giving the deciding factors.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. List your services and what each depends on.\n2. Which user journeys are most critical?\n3. Which dependencies are third-party?\nProceed after I respond.",
