    "id": "a3e65e70-7442-5ea9-b8ed-5f0b1e79a0ba",
    "title": "Data: Database-per-Service Migration Plan",
    "description": "Plans how to split a shared database into per-service databases with data synchronization, consistency choices, and cutover steps.",
    "rawContent": "Create a step-by-step plan to break my shared database into one database per service.\n \nUse this structure:\n- Current coupling analysis: tables, foreign keys, and cross-service joins found\n- Target ownership: which service owns which tables\n- Replacement for joins: API calls, data replication, or materialized views (choose and justify)\n- Consistency decisions: where eventual consistency is acceptable and where it is not\n- Cutover sequence: numbered steps with a rollback for each\n- Validation: how to prove the data matches before and after\n \n### Rules:\n- Handle foreign keys explicitly; never ignore them.\n- Include a dual-write or change-data-capture option and compare them in a short table.\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me:\n1. Which database and how large is it?\n2. Paste your table list or schema summary.\n3. Which services will own which parts, if known?\n4. How much downtime is allowed?\nAnswer and I will begin.",
