    "title": "Documentation: Architecture Overview for Stakeholders",
    "description": "Converts a technical microservices design into a clear stakeholder overview with diagrams-in-text, risks, costs, and timeline in plain language.",
    "rawContent": "Translate my technical architecture into a document that managers and non-technical stakeholders can understand.\n \nStructure:\n1. The goal in one paragraph (no technical terms)\n2. How it works, explained with a real-world analogy\n3. Simple diagram in text form using boxes and arrows\n4. What changes for users and for staff\n5. Risks in plain words, each with a mitigation\n6. Cost and timeline summary table\n7. Decisions we need from stakeholders\n \n### Rules:\n- Reading level: a smart person who has never coded.\n- Maximum 2 pages.\n- Replace every technical term with a plain word, or explain it in brackets once.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste or describe the architecture.\n2. Who is the audience and what do they care about?\n3. Do you have cost and timeline numbers?\nThen write it.\nRow 4: Unit Testing Suite Generator\nCategory: Development & Coding | Prompts 1 to 20",
