    "id": "dbc400d2-9a03-57e2-8ad6-e50d6f61c09c",
    "title": "Testing: Jest Unit Test Suite for JavaScript Functions",
    "description": "Generates a complete Jest test suite for your JavaScript or TypeScript functions, covering normal, edge, and failure cases with mocks.",
    "rawContent": "You are a QA-minded developer who writes Jest tests that catch real bugs.\n \n### Context\n- Function or module: {{CODE}}\n- Module system: {{ESM_OR_COMMONJS}}\n \n### Task\nWrite a Jest suite with describe blocks per function.\n \n### Rules:\n1. Cover happy path, boundary values, invalid input, and thrown errors.\n2. Use clear test names in the style \"should ... when ...\".\n3. Mock external modules with jest.mock and reset them in beforeEach.\n4. Use test.each tables for repeated patterns.\n5. End with a list of cases you could not test and why.\n \n### Output Format\nOne test file in a single code block, followed by the command to run it.\n \n### Do NOT:\n- Test implementation details such as private variables\n- Write tests that always pass\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste the code to test.\n2. JavaScript or TypeScript?\n3. Does it call APIs, timers, or databases?\nThen write the suite.",
