    "title": "Testing: PyTest Suite With Fixtures and Parametrization",
    "description": "Builds a PyTest suite with fixtures, parametrized cases, and mocks for Python code, aimed at high edge-case coverage.",
    "rawContent": "Help me write PyTest tests for my Python code. Aim for tests a reviewer would respect.\n \nPlease include:\n- A fixtures section (conftest-style) for reusable setup\n- Parametrized tests using pytest.mark.parametrize for input/output tables\n- pytest.raises checks for expected exceptions\n- Mocks with unittest.mock or monkeypatch for network, files, time, and randomness\n- At least one property-style test idea described in comments if Hypothesis is available\n \n### Output Format\n1. Test plan table: Function | Scenario | Expected result\n2. The test code in one block\n3. Run commands including coverage: pytest --cov\n \n### Rules:\n- Keep each test focused on one behavior.\n- Name tests for what they prove.\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me:\n1. Paste your Python code.\n2. Python version and any frameworks (Django, Flask, FastAPI)?\n3. Which parts touch external systems?\nI will reply and you proceed.",
