    "id": "fe6b0281-4145-5e86-8e50-95e7453b1007",
    "title": "Testing: JUnit 5 Suite With Mockito",
    "description": "Creates JUnit 5 tests with Mockito for Java classes, including exception tests, verification of interactions, and parameterized tests.",
    "rawContent": "As an experienced Java engineer, write unit tests with JUnit 5 and Mockito for the class I give you.\n \nRequired elements:\n1. @ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class) with @Mock and @InjectMocks\n2. Nested test classes grouped by method\n3. @ParameterizedTest with @CsvSource or @MethodSource for input variety\n4. assertThrows for error paths\n5. verify() calls for important interactions, and verifyNoMoreInteractions where sensible\n6. ArgumentCaptor where values passed to collaborators matter\n \n### Do NOT:\n- Use PowerMock\n- Test getters and setters with no logic\n- Rely on test execution order\n \nAfter the code, list the Maven or Gradle command to run it and any dependencies to add.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste the class and its collaborators' signatures.\n2. Java and Spring versions?\n3. Any business rules I should know that are not obvious from code?\nThen write the tests.",
