    "title": "Coverage: Edge Case Brainstormer for Any Function",
    "description": "Brainstorms a thorough list of edge cases and failure scenarios for a function before any test code is written.",
    "rawContent": "Before I write tests, think like a mischievous user. Find ways my function can break.\n \nGroup your ideas under these headings:\n- Empty and null inputs\n- Boundary values (min, max, off-by-one)\n- Wrong types and malformed data\n- Very large or very small inputs\n- Special characters, Unicode, and whitespace\n- Time, date, and time zone traps\n- Concurrency or repeated calls\n- External failure (timeouts, missing files)\n \nFor each idea give a concrete input and the expected behavior, written in one line.\n \nAt the end, mark the 5 cases most likely to reveal a real bug.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste the function.\n2. What should it do in plain words?\n3. Who calls it and with what kind of data?\nI will answer, then you brainstorm.",
