    "title": "Fixtures: Test Data Builder and Factory Generator",
    "description": "Creates reusable test data builders and factories so tests stay short, readable, and independent of irrelevant details.",
    "rawContent": "My tests are full of repetitive setup code. Create test data builders for my domain objects.\n \nDeliver:\n1. A builder or factory for each object I list, with sensible valid defaults.\n2. Fluent override methods (for example anOrder().withStatus(\"PAID\").build()).\n3. Helpers for common variants (valid, invalid, minimal, maximal).\n4. Randomized values only where it helps, using a seeded generator for repeatability.\n5. Two before/after test examples showing how much shorter they become.\n \n### Rules:\n- Defaults must produce a valid object so each test overrides only what it cares about.\n- Do not hide the important values from the test body.\n \nUse {{LANGUAGE}} idioms.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste the classes or data structures.\n2. Paste one existing test with messy setup.\n3. Which language and test framework?\nBegin after I answer.",
