    "id": "f0b207c9-111f-5da9-ad38-ce261c17bc29",
    "title": "Async: Testing Timers, Promises, and Event-Driven Code",
    "description": "Shows how to reliably test asynchronous code, timeouts, retries, and event emitters without sleeping or flaky waits.",
    "rawContent": "Write reliable tests for my asynchronous code. No arbitrary sleeps are allowed.\n \nCover:\n- Resolved and rejected promises\n- Timeouts and debounce using fake timers (advance time explicitly)\n- Retry logic with exponential backoff: assert the number of attempts and delays\n- Event emitters and callbacks: assert event order and payload\n- Race conditions between two async calls\n- Cleanup: no leaked timers or open handles\n \n### Output Format\n1. Short explanation of the strategy for each async pattern found in my code\n2. Test code in one block\n3. A checklist for spotting flaky async tests\n \n### Do NOT: use real network or setTimeout waits.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste the async code.\n2. Language and test framework?\n3. Which behaviors have been flaky before?\nThen write them.",
