    "description": "Adds micro-benchmarks and performance regression guards around critical functions without making the test suite flaky.",
    "rawContent": "Add performance guards for my critical functions without creating flaky tests.\n \nPlan:\n1. Choose which functions deserve benchmarks (list criteria and apply them to my code).\n2. Write benchmarks with the right tool for {{LANGUAGE}} (warm-up, multiple iterations, realistic input sizes).\n3. Replace absolute time assertions with relative checks or complexity checks (for example, doubling the input should not quadruple the time).\n4. Where to run them: separate CI job, not with fast unit tests.\n5. How to store results and detect regressions over time (thresholds and noise tolerance).\n6. Common mistakes: dead-code elimination, cold starts, noisy machines.\n \n### Output Format\nShort sections with code blocks.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Which functions are performance-critical and what are the targets?\n2. Language and CI system?\n3. Typical input sizes?\nBegin after I answer.\nRow 5: API Documentation Generator (Swagger/OpenAPI)\nCategory: Development & Coding | Prompts 1 to 20",
