    "rawContent": "Write the reference documentation text for my API in the voice of a helpful developer-relations writer. Audience: developers integrating for the first time.\n \nFor each endpoint use this exact layout:\n### [METHOD] /path\nWhat it does (one sentence)\nWhen to use it\nParameters (table: Name | In | Type | Required | Description)\nExample request (curl)\nExample response (JSON)\nErrors (table: Code | Meaning | How to fix)\nNotes (rate limits, pagination, gotchas)\n \n### Rules:\n- Present tense, active voice, no marketing language.\n- Never explain the same concept twice; link back instead.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste the endpoints or your OpenAPI file.\n2. Base URL and authentication method?\n3. Any rate limits?\nThen write the docs.",
