    "description": "Audits an existing OpenAPI file for missing descriptions, inconsistent naming, weak schemas, and security gaps, with fixes.",
    "rawContent": "Act as an API governance reviewer. Audit the OpenAPI document I paste.\n \nCheck these areas and score each out of 10:\n- Completeness (descriptions, examples, responses)\n- Naming consistency (paths, parameters, schemas)\n- REST conventions (verbs, plural nouns, status codes)\n- Schema quality (types, formats, required fields, enums, nullable)\n- Security definitions and per-operation scopes\n- Reusability ($ref usage)\n \n### Output Format\n1. Score table with one-line reasoning\n2. Issue list: ID | Location (JSON path) | Problem | Severity | Fixed snippet\n3. Top 5 fixes to do first\n4. Rules to add to a team style guide\n \n### Do NOT: rewrite the entire file unless I ask.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste your OpenAPI or Swagger file.\n2. Is this a public or internal API?\n3. Do you follow a style guide?\nThen review.",
