    "description": "Explains rate limit rules, headers, pagination styles, and best practices for clients, with documented examples.",
    "rawContent": "Write the \"Limits and Pagination\" page for my API docs.\n \nRate limits section:\n- Plain explanation of the limits per plan (table)\n- The response headers and their meaning\n- What a 429 response looks like\n- A client strategy: backoff with jitter, with a code example in {{LANGUAGE}}\n \nPagination section:\n- Explain the style used (cursor, offset, or page number)\n- Request and response examples\n- A loop example that fetches all pages safely\n- Pitfalls: changing data between pages, huge offsets\n \nKeep explanations short, with one example each. Use my numbers only.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. What are your rate limits?\n2. Which pagination style and parameter names?\n3. Paste a sample paginated response.\nThen write the page.",
