    "id": "ae5cdd5d-d904-5a16-b548-ea1c64b840a6",
    "title": "API Docs: Docs-as-Code Pipeline Setup",
    "description": "Sets up a docs-as-code pipeline that lints, builds, and publishes OpenAPI docs automatically from your repository.",
    "rawContent": "Design a docs-as-code setup so API documentation never goes out of date.\n \nProvide:\n1. Repository layout (where the spec, examples, and guides live)\n2. Lint step with Spectral and a starter ruleset (10 rules with reasons)\n3. Build step to produce a static site with {{DOC_TOOL}} (Redoc, Swagger UI, or Stoplight)\n4. CI workflow file for {{CI_SYSTEM}} that lints, builds, and deploys on merge\n5. A check that fails the build if code routes and spec drift apart\n6. Pull request template with a documentation checklist\n7. Versioned docs strategy\n \n### Output Format\nFile tree, then each file's content in its own code block.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Language/framework of the API?\n2. CI system and hosting for docs?\n3. Is the spec hand-written or generated from code?\nThen build it.",
