    "id": "a1b9296e-9c7d-5d8e-968a-af88ff0acad3",
    "title": "API Docs: Migration Guide From Another API",
    "description": "Writes a migration guide for developers moving from a competitor or older API, mapping old calls to new ones side by side.",
    "rawContent": "Write a migration guide for developers switching to my API from {{OLD_API}}.\n \nStructure:\n1. Why migrate and what improves (3 honest bullets)\n2. Concept mapping table: Old concept | New concept | Notes\n3. Endpoint mapping table: Old call | New call | Differences\n4. Side-by-side code: Before and After for the 5 most common tasks\n5. Authentication changes\n6. Data migration steps and a testing checklist\n7. Parallel-run strategy and rollback advice\n8. Gaps: features the new API does not have yet\n \n### Rules:\n- Be honest about gaps. Do not oversell.\n- Only describe the old API using details I provide.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Which API are developers leaving?\n2. Paste both API endpoint lists or specs.\n3. What are the most common tasks users do?\nThen write the guide.",
