    "rawContent": "Draft an \"API Usage Policy\" page in plain language that developers will actually read. It is documentation, not legal advice.\n \nInclude these sections with short headings:\n- Who can use the API\n- Fair use and quotas (use my numbers)\n- What is not allowed\n- Support levels and response times\n- Uptime commitments (only as I state them)\n- Deprecation and change notice period\n- How to report problems or abuse\n \n### Rules:\n- Short sentences. No legalese.\n- Use \"TBD\" for anything I did not provide.\n \nHave a lawyer review this before publishing.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe your API and users.\n2. Your quotas, support, and uptime commitments?\n3. Notice period for breaking changes?\nThen draft it.",
