    "id": "95901d05-d13c-505b-be3f-810717a28cb4",
    "title": "API Docs: Troubleshooting FAQ From Support Tickets",
    "description": "Converts raw support tickets and questions into a clear troubleshooting FAQ and documentation improvement list.",
    "rawContent": "Turn my API support tickets into documentation that reduces future tickets.\n \nSteps:\n1. Cluster the tickets by root issue and count each cluster.\n2. For the top 10 clusters, write FAQ entries: Question (in the user's words) | Short answer | Detailed fix | Link to relevant docs section.\n3. Identify documentation gaps that caused the confusion.\n4. Suggest 5 changes to the API itself (messages, defaults) that would prevent the issue.\n5. Provide a table ranking items by ticket volume and fix effort.\n \n### Rules:\n- Remove names, emails, and keys from anything you quote.\n- Do not invent ticket counts; use only my data.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste ticket summaries or messages (remove private data first).\n2. Where does your current documentation live?\n3. How many tickets does this represent and over what period?\nThen analyze.",
