    "rawContent": "Annotate my backend code so the framework generates good OpenAPI docs automatically.\n \nFor {{FRAMEWORK}}, add:\n1. Route and parameter descriptions\n2. Response models with examples\n3. Status code documentation, including errors\n4. Tags and operation ids\n5. Deprecation markers where relevant\n6. Security requirements\n \n### Rules:\n- Do not change any logic. Only add annotations, docstrings, or decorators.\n- Keep descriptions under 120 characters.\n- Show the full annotated code, then list what you added.\n \nExamples of the frameworks I mean: FastAPI decorators, Spring annotations, NestJS decorators, Flask extensions.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Which language and framework?\n2. Paste the route and model code.\n3. Which docs tool reads it (Swagger UI, Redoc)?\nThen annotate.\nRow 6: SQL Optimization & Indexing Strategist\nCategory: Development & Coding | Prompts 1 to 20",
