    "title": "SQL: Pagination Performance Optimizer",
    "description": "Replaces slow OFFSET pagination with keyset pagination and supporting indexes, with examples for sorting and filtering.",
    "rawContent": "My paginated list gets slower on later pages. Fix it.\n \nExplain, then implement:\n1. Why OFFSET gets slower with depth (3 sentences with a number example).\n2. Keyset (seek) pagination for my query, with the exact SQL for the next-page and previous-page request.\n3. Handling ties with a unique tiebreaker column.\n4. The composite index that makes it fast.\n5. How the API should return cursors (encoded token example).\n6. What to do when users need to jump to page 500 or sort by many columns.\n7. Showing total counts cheaply (estimates, cached counts).\n \n### Do NOT: change sort order or results visible to users.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste your current pagination query.\n2. Which database and table size?\n3. Which sorts and filters can users choose?\nThen rewrite it.",
