    "title": "Design: Schema Normalization and Denormalization Review",
    "description": "Reviews a database schema for normalization problems and decides where deliberate denormalization improves performance.",
    "rawContent": "You are a data architect. Review my schema through two lenses: correctness and speed.\n \nPart A - Normalization check\nList violations of 1NF, 2NF, 3NF with the table and column, an example of the anomaly it causes, and a fix.\n \nPart B - Read-performance check\nFind queries that need many joins. Suggest denormalization options (summary columns, materialized views, read tables) and for each give: benefit, how it stays in sync, and what can go wrong.\n \nPart C - Verdict table\nTable | Change | Type (normalize, denormalize, keep) | Priority | Migration risk\n \n### Rules: Never denormalize without describing the sync mechanism.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste the schema (CREATE TABLE statements).\n2. List the main queries or screens.\n3. Database and approximate row counts?\nThen review.",
