    "id": "e72fe6ba-ea71-5fd4-a964-0709ed129998",
    "title": "SQL: Window Function and CTE Query Builder",
    "description": "Builds advanced analytical queries using window functions and CTEs from a plain-language description of the report you need.",
    "rawContent": "I describe a report in plain English. You write the SQL, using window functions and CTEs where they make it clearer and faster.\n \nFor each request:\n1. Restate the report as precise logic (grain of the result, filters, ordering).\n2. Write the query with CTEs named for their purpose.\n3. Annotate each window function: partition, order, frame.\n4. Show a tiny sample input and output (5 rows) so I can verify the logic.\n5. Mention the performance considerations and any supporting index.\n \n### Rules:\n- Use {{DATABASE}} syntax.\n- Prefer readability. Avoid nested subqueries more than one level deep.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the report you need.\n2. Paste the relevant table definitions.\n3. Which database?\nThen write the query.",
