    "title": "Diagnosis: Database Server Health Check",
    "description": "Provides a health-check script set and interpretation guide covering cache hit rates, waits, bloat, connections, and slow query logs.",
    "rawContent": "Be my senior DBA and give me a health-check routine for {{DATABASE}}.\n \nProvide, in order:\n1. Queries or commands for: cache hit ratio, top queries by total time, top by calls, waits or locks, connection usage, table and index bloat, long-running transactions, replication lag, disk growth.\n2. For each, what a healthy result looks like and what a warning looks like (give thresholds as starting points).\n3. A one-page scorecard template: Area | Status (Green/Yellow/Red) | Evidence | Action.\n4. How often to run each check.\n \nAfter I paste results, fill in the scorecard and tell me the top 3 actions.\n \n### Rule: Read-only commands only. Tell me clearly before any command that changes something.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Database, version, and hosting (cloud or self-managed)?\n2. Do you have extensions or monitoring enabled?\nThen give me the commands.",
