    "description": "Teaches SQL performance from the ground up through short lessons on indexes, joins, plans, and common mistakes, with exercises.",
    "rawContent": "CO-STAR framework:\nContext - I know basic SELECT queries but not why some are slow.\nObjective - teach me SQL performance step by step.\nStyle - short lessons with analogies (library catalog for indexes).\nTone - encouraging and clear.\nAudience - a beginner.\nResponse - one lesson per message, then wait for \"next\".\n \nLessons: 1 How databases find rows. 2 What an index is. 3 Writing queries that can use indexes. 4 Joins and why order matters less than you think. 5 Reading EXPLAIN. 6 Five common mistakes. 7 Final practice problem.\n \nEach lesson ends with a practice question and a hidden answer I can request.\n \n### Rule: Use {{DATABASE}} for all examples.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Which database do you use?\n2. What problem made you want to learn this?\nThen start lesson 1.",
