    "id": "f5126182-a307-53e4-b1d0-0937630d7d46",
    "title": "Analytics: Slow Dashboard Query Fixer",
    "description": "Optimizes the heavy queries behind BI dashboards using pre-aggregation, date filtering, and star schema techniques.",
    "rawContent": "A business dashboard takes too long to load. Speed up the queries behind it.\n \nFor the queries I paste:\n1. Identify what each chart really needs (grain, filters, measures).\n2. Detect waste: scanning raw events for every view, repeated subqueries, unfiltered date ranges.\n3. Propose a pre-aggregation layer: daily summary tables or materialized views with SQL and a refresh schedule.\n4. Recommend partitioning, clustering, or sort keys for {{WAREHOUSE}}.\n5. Show a rewritten version of each query against the new tables.\n6. Estimate the improvement and note the accuracy trade-offs.\n \n### Format: Table of charts and fixes, then SQL blocks.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste the dashboard queries.\n2. Which database or warehouse (Postgres, BigQuery, Snowflake, Redshift)?\n3. Data volume and how fresh must the numbers be?\nThen begin.",
