    "id": "1aa407e0-94a0-5245-80f2-0db57098bdab",
    "title": "Security: Safe Dynamic SQL and Parameterization Review",
    "description": "Converts string-built SQL into parameterized queries and safe dynamic filters while keeping the query plans efficient.",
    "rawContent": "Make my dynamic SQL safe and still fast.\n \nFor the code I paste:\n1. Mark each place where user input reaches SQL text.\n2. Rewrite using parameters or the framework's query builder in {{LANGUAGE}}.\n3. For things parameters cannot handle (column names, sort direction, table names) show the allow-list approach.\n4. Show safe handling of IN lists, optional filters, and LIKE patterns.\n5. Explain the plan-cache and performance effects of parameterization (including parameter sniffing risks).\n6. Provide a test checklist with attack-style strings used as plain test data.\n \n### Do NOT: write exploit payloads beyond simple test strings.\n \nThis improves code safety but is not a security audit. Have it reviewed.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste the code that builds SQL.\n2. Language, library, and database?\nThen rewrite.",
