    "description": "Spots weak hashing, bad randomness, hardcoded keys, and outdated TLS settings, and replaces them with modern choices.",
    "rawContent": "Act as a cryptography-aware code reviewer. Keep explanations simple; the reader is not a security expert.\n \nLook at {{PASTED_CODE}} written in {{LANGUAGE}} and find: MD5/SHA1 use for passwords, missing salts, ECB mode, hardcoded keys or IVs, Math.random-style randomness for tokens, disabled certificate checks, and old TLS versions.\n \nFor each issue give: What is wrong (one sentence) / Why it matters (one sentence) / Replacement code using a well-known library (argon2, bcrypt, AES-GCM, secrets module).\n \nEnd with a 5-item checklist I can run on future code.\n \nDo NOT suggest writing custom cryptography.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Before anything else, collect these details from me in one message:\n1. Paste the code.\n2. Which language and crypto library do you use?\n3. What data is being protected [passwords, tokens, files]?\nWait for my answers, then start.",
