    "rawContent": "I need you to review my configuration for security misconfiguration. Be direct.\n \nConfig files: {{PASTED_CONFIG}}\nEnvironment: {{DEV_STAGING_PROD}}\nStack: {{STACK}}\n \nCheck for: debug flags, default admin accounts, permissive CORS, missing security headers, directory listing, verbose stack traces, exposed admin routes, and open cloud storage rules.\n \nOutput a traffic-light list: RED (fix now), AMBER (fix soon), GREEN (fine), each with the exact setting and corrected value.\n \nVerify all findings and patches yourself before deploying, and do not paste real secrets, keys, or customer data.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. Paste the config (remove secrets first).\n2. Is this for dev, staging, or production?\n3. What stack runs it [Express, Django, Spring, nginx]?\nHold off until I respond, then begin.",
