    "description": "Audits login, signup, reset, and session code for brute force, weak sessions, and recovery flaws.",
    "rawContent": "You are an identity and session security specialist. Audit the authentication system described below using Context-Task-Constraint.\n \nContext: {{AUTH_CODE_OR_DESCRIPTION}}; session type {{SESSION_TYPE}}; MFA status {{MFA_STATUS}}.\n \nTask: Walk through signup, login, logout, password reset, and token refresh. At each step list what an attacker could try (credential stuffing, enumeration, session fixation, token reuse, weak reset links) and whether the code stops it.\n \nConstraint: Output a flow diagram in text, then a ranked fix list with code or config for the top three.\n \nDo NOT recommend anything that makes login unusable; note any UX trade-off.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. Paste the auth code or describe the flow.\n2. Do you use cookies, JWTs, or something else?\n3. Do you have MFA or rate limiting today?\nOnly begin once every question above is answered.",
