    "description": "Finds unsafe deserialization, unsigned updates, and trust in untrusted data, and proposes safe alternatives.",
    "rawContent": "Examine this code only for data and software integrity failures.\n \nCode: {{PASTED_CODE}}\nLanguage: {{LANGUAGE}}\nWhere the data comes from: {{DATA_SOURCE}}\n \nLook for: pickle/yaml.load/ObjectInputStream style deserialization of untrusted input, unsigned auto-updates, CI plugins pulled without pinning, and cookies or JSON blobs trusted without a signature.\n \nAnswer in this shape:\n- Finding\n- Why it can lead to code execution or tampering (plain words)\n- Safe replacement (JSON with schema validation, signed payloads, allow-lists)\n- Test to confirm the fix\n \nIf nothing risky is present, say so; do not pad.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Before anything else, collect these details from me in one message:\n1. Paste the code.\n2. Language and library used?\n3. Who or what sends the data [users, other services, files]?\nBegin only after I answer.",
