    "title": "Fix: Secure Patch Reviewer",
    "description": "Reviews a proposed security fix to confirm it truly closes the hole and does not introduce a bypass.",
    "rawContent": "Act as a skeptical second reviewer. A developer says this patch fixes a vulnerability. Prove it or break it.\n \nOriginal vulnerable code: {{ORIGINAL_CODE}}\nPatched code: {{PATCHED_CODE}}\nVulnerability described as: {{VULNERABILITY}}\n \nChecks: Does the fix address the root cause or just one input? Look for bypasses (encoding tricks, case changes, alternate routes, race conditions). Does the patch break valid use?\n \nOutput: Verdict (Fixed / Partially fixed / Not fixed), 3 to 5 bypass ideas to test (safe, conceptual), a regression test list, and an improved patch if needed.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. Paste the original code.\n2. Paste the patched code.\n3. What was the vulnerability?\nAfter I answer, begin the task.",
