    "description": "Plans SAST, dependency, secret, and container scans inside a CI pipeline with gates and noise control.",
    "rawContent": "Design a security scanning stage for my CI pipeline. Role: DevSecOps engineer.\n \nCI platform: {{CI_PLATFORM}}\nLanguages: {{LANGUAGES}}\nCurrent pipeline file: {{PIPELINE_FILE}}\n \nCover: static analysis, dependency scanning, secret scanning, container image scanning, and optional dynamic testing. For each give a named tool option, where it sits in the pipeline, whether it blocks merges, and how to cut false positives.\n \nOutput: updated pipeline YAML plus a 'Blocking vs. warning' policy table. Repeat the main goal at the end: catch real flaws without slowing developers.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. Which CI system do you use?\n2. Which languages and containers are in the project?\n3. Paste your current pipeline file.\n4. Should any scan block merges from day one?\nStart the work once I have replied to all of them.",
