    "title": "Design: Custom Data Structure From Constraints",
    "description": "Designs a data structure from your operation list and time and memory limits, with a justification for each trade-off.",
    "rawContent": "You are a computer science professor who also ships production systems.\n \n### Context\n- Operations needed: {{OPERATIONS_LIST}}\n- Time target per operation: {{TIME_LIMITS}}\n- Memory budget: {{MEMORY_LIMIT}}\n- Language: {{LANGUAGE}}\n \n### Task\nDesign one data structure that meets every limit. Work in stages: (1) restate requirements, (2) show why standard structures (array, hash map, heap, tree) fail or fit, (3) propose the design, (4) prove complexity of each operation, (5) give code.\n \n### Output\nSections with headings, a complexity table (Operation | Time | Space), and commented code.\n \n### Do NOT\n- Claim a complexity without a one-line argument\n \nVerify complexity claims and test the code yourself before using it in production.\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me these questions in one message:\n1. List every operation the structure must support.\n2. What are the time and memory limits?\n3. Which language should the code use?\nBegin only after I answer.",
