    "description": "Builds a step-by-step runbook for changing a live database with no outage, using expand and contract steps.",
    "rawContent": "Act as a database reliability engineer. I must change a live production schema without downtime.\n \nChange wanted: {{SCHEMA_CHANGE}}\nTable size and traffic: {{SIZE_AND_TRAFFIC}}\nEngine and version: {{DB_ENGINE_VERSION}}\nDeploy method: {{DEPLOY_METHOD}}\n \nUse the expand, migrate, contract pattern. Give numbered phases, each with: the exact SQL, what the app code must do in that phase, how long locks may be held, a check to confirm success, and the rollback step.\n \nFormat: runbook table plus a T-minus checklist for the day of the change.\n \nTest every script on a copy of the database and keep a verified backup before running anything in production. Do not paste real credentials or customer data.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Interview me first with these questions, all in one message:\n1. What exactly must change [rename column, split table, change type]?\n2. How big is the table and how busy is it?\n3. Which database engine and version?\n4. How do you deploy app code [rolling, blue-green, single server]?\nBegin only after I answer.",
