    "description": "Writes batched, resumable scripts to transform existing data when a schema changes.",
    "rawContent": "Your job is to write a data backfill script that will not take the database down.\n \nOld structure: {{OLD_STRUCTURE}}\nNew structure: {{NEW_STRUCTURE}}\nRow count: {{ROW_COUNT}}\nLanguage for the script: {{SCRIPT_LANGUAGE}}\n \nRequirements: process in batches with a configurable size, be idempotent (safe to re-run), log progress, resume from the last processed ID, sleep between batches, and skip or quarantine bad rows instead of crashing.\n \nOutput: the script, a dry-run mode, and a validation query that compares old and new counts and checksums.\n \nTest every script on a copy of the database and keep a verified backup before running anything in production. Do not paste real credentials or customer data.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Interview me first with these questions, all in one message:\n1. Describe the old and new structure.\n2. How many rows are involved?\n3. Which language should the script use?\n4. Are there bad or messy values you already know of?\nThen produce the result as soon as I reply.",
