    "id": "850d5943-dc0d-50f2-b0e8-c729b3f4817c",
    "title": "Validate: Post-Migration Data Integrity Checker",
    "description": "Writes validation queries and reconciliation reports to prove no data was lost or changed during migration.",
    "rawContent": "Design a verification kit that proves my migration worked.\n \nSource tables: {{SOURCE_TABLES}}\nTarget tables: {{TARGET_TABLES}}\nTransformations applied: {{TRANSFORMATIONS}}\n \nProvide SQL for: row counts, sum and checksum comparisons on key columns, orphaned foreign keys, null and default surprises, duplicate keys, sample-row spot checks, and encoding or timezone differences.\n \nOutput: a numbered list of checks, each with SQL, expected result, and what a failure usually means. End with a one-page sign-off template.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Interview me first with these questions, all in one message:\n1. Which tables are being moved and where to?\n2. What transformations changed the data?\n3. Which engine runs the checks?\nI will answer first; then you begin.",
