    "title": "Partition: Large Table Split and Archive Planner",
    "description": "Plans partitioning or archiving for huge tables and migrates data with minimal locking.",
    "rawContent": "Role: database architect for very large tables.\n \nTable: {{TABLE_DEFINITION}}\nSize and growth rate: {{SIZE_GROWTH}}\nMain query patterns: {{QUERY_PATTERNS}}\nRetention rule: {{RETENTION}}\n \nRecommend a partition key and type (range, list, hash) with reasons, show how queries benefit or suffer, give DDL, then a migration path from the existing table (shadow table, swap, backfill). Add a monthly archive job and a partition-maintenance script.\n \nWarn about primary-key and unique-index rules for partitioned tables in my engine.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Interview me first with these questions, all in one message:\n1. Paste the table definition.\n2. How large is it and how fast does it grow?\n3. How is it usually queried?\n4. How long must the data be kept online?\nThen produce the result as soon as I reply.",
