    "description": "Plans moving from one shared database to per-tenant schemas or databases, with routing and data separation.",
    "rawContent": "Help me split a shared multi-tenant database safely.\n \nCurrent approach: {{CURRENT_TENANCY}}\nNumber of tenants and largest tenant size: {{TENANT_STATS}}\nGoal: {{GOAL}} (isolation, performance, compliance)\n \nCompare: shared tables with tenant_id, schema per tenant, database per tenant. Recommend one. Then provide: tenant data extraction SQL, load process, connection routing approach, migration order (small tenants first), and a per-tenant verification step.\n \nFormat: comparison table then numbered plan.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me all of the following in a single message:\n1. How are tenants separated today?\n2. How many tenants do you have and how big is the largest?\n3. Why do you want to split [security, speed, customer demand]?\nStart the work once I have replied to all of them.",
