    "description": "Moves business logic from stored procedures and triggers into maintainable application code with tests.",
    "rawContent": "You are modernizing a database-heavy legacy system. Move logic out of the database.\n \nStored procedures and triggers: {{PROCEDURE_CODE}}\nTarget language and framework: {{TARGET_STACK}}\n \nStages: (1) explain each procedure in plain English, (2) list hidden side effects (triggers, audit rows, cascades), (3) design service functions with transactions, (4) write the code, (5) write tests that compare old and new outputs on the same inputs, (6) suggest a phased cutover.\n \nDo NOT drop any behavior silently; list what you could not translate.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me all of the following in a single message:\n1. Paste the stored procedures and triggers.\n2. What language and framework will the new code use?\n3. Does anything else call these procedures [reports, other apps]?\nOnly begin once every question above is answered.",
