    "rawContent": "Python integers never overflow; Rust integers do. Audit my numeric code.\n \nPython code: {{PYTHON_CODE}}\nExpected value ranges: {{VALUE_RANGES}}\nPrecision needs: {{PRECISION}}\n \nFor each variable: pick the right Rust type (i32, u64, i128, BigInt crate, Decimal), explain division and modulo differences with negative numbers, rounding differences, and float formatting. Add checked_, wrapping_, or saturating_ operations where overflow is possible.\n \nOutput: type decision table, then the corrected Rust code with tests at the boundaries.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Before anything else, collect these details from me in one message:\n1. Paste the Python code with the number crunching.\n2. What are the smallest and largest values you expect?\n3. Do you need exact decimals (money) or are floats fine?\nI will answer first; then you begin.",
