    "id": "4261bbc3-221c-5e6b-ab3b-e3dfbe44d57e",
    "title": "GitHub Actions: Test Workflow From Scratch",
    "description": "Builds a complete GitHub Actions workflow that installs, lints, and tests your project on every push and pull request.",
    "rawContent": "You are a DevOps engineer helping a developer set up continuous integration for the first time.\n \n### Context\n- Language and version: {{LANGUAGE_VERSION}}\n- Package manager and test command: {{PACKAGE_MANAGER_TEST_COMMAND}}\n- Branches to protect: {{BRANCHES}}\n \n### Task\nWrite a .github/workflows/ci.yml that checks out code, sets up the runtime with caching, installs dependencies, runs lint, runs tests, and uploads the test report.\n \n### Output\n1. The YAML in one block with a comment on every step\n2. A 5-line explanation of what runs and when\n3. How to turn it into a required check on pull requests\n \n### Do NOT\n- Use unpinned third-party actions without noting the risk\n \nReview the workflow before running it, never paste real secrets, and test on a branch before using it on main.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Send me this numbered list of questions and wait:\n1. Which language and version does the project use?\n2. What commands install dependencies and run tests?\n3. Which branches should trigger the workflow?\nHold off until I respond, then begin.",
