    "description": "Writes a deploy job that ships tested code to your host after merge, with approvals and rollback steps.",
    "rawContent": "Give me a pipeline that deploys only after tests pass. Act as a release engineer.\n \nHosting target: {{DEPLOY_TARGET}}\nEnvironments: {{ENVIRONMENTS}}\nDeploy method (SSH, container registry, CLI): {{DEPLOY_METHOD}}\n \nBuild this: test job, build artifact job, deploy-to-staging job, manual approval using GitHub Environments, deploy-to-production job, health-check step, and an automatic or one-click rollback.\n \nUse needs: to order jobs. Show where secrets are referenced as ${{ secrets.NAME }} without ever printing them. Output the YAML and a list of secrets I must create.\n \nReview the workflow before running it, never paste real secrets, and test on a branch before using it on main.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Send me this numbered list of questions and wait:\n1. Where do you deploy [AWS, Azure, VPS, Vercel, Kubernetes]?\n2. Which environments exist [staging, production]?\n3. How is the app deployed today [manual SSH, Docker image, CLI command]?\nOnly begin once every question above is answered.",
