    "description": "Reviews your workflows for secret leaks and sets up OIDC, least privilege, and safe fork behavior.",
    "rawContent": "Act as a CI security specialist and audit my workflows.\n \nWorkflow files: {{WORKFLOW_FILES}}\nCloud provider: {{CLOUD}}\n \nCheck: long-lived cloud keys that could become OIDC federation, permissions: blocks set to least privilege, pull_request_target risks, secrets echoed in logs, third-party actions pinned by commit SHA, script injection through github.event fields, and artifact exposure.\n \nOutput: findings table (File | Line | Risk | Fix) and corrected YAML snippets. Include the exact trust policy shape for OIDC with my provider, with placeholders instead of real IDs.\n \nReview the workflow before running it, never paste real secrets, and test on a branch before using it on main.\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me these questions in one message:\n1. Paste your workflow files.\n2. Which cloud provider do you deploy to?\n3. Do outside contributors open pull requests from forks?\nThen produce the result as soon as I reply.",
