    "title": "Preview: Pull Request Preview Environments",
    "description": "Creates per-pull-request preview deployments with automatic comments and cleanup on close.",
    "rawContent": "Design ephemeral preview environments for each pull request.\n \nApp type: {{APP_TYPE}}\nHosting option: {{HOSTING}}\nDatabase needs: {{DATABASE_NEEDS}}\n \nBuild workflows triggered on opened, synchronize, and closed events. They must: deploy to a unique URL based on the PR number, seed data safely, comment the URL on the pull request, update on each push, and tear everything down when the PR closes or goes stale after 7 days.\n \nAdd cost guards and a note on never giving preview environments production secrets. Output YAML and a cleanup scheduled job.\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me these questions in one message:\n1. What type of app is it [static site, API, full-stack]?\n2. Where would previews be hosted?\n3. Does the app need a database or other services?\nI will answer first; then you begin.",
