    "description": "Adds useful, low-noise notifications for failures, deployments, and flaky tests.",
    "rawContent": "Write something that makes my pipeline tell me what matters and nothing else.\n \nNotification channel: {{CHANNEL}}\nEvents I care about: {{EVENTS}}\nTeam members to mention: {{WHO_TO_NOTIFY}}\n \nCreate workflow steps that post: failed main-branch builds (mention the commit author), successful production deploys (with version and link), and a weekly summary of failed runs. Use if: failure() and if: success() correctly. Avoid noise: no messages for pull request drafts.\n \nShow the message layout as plain text and the YAML to send it.\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me these questions in one message:\n1. Where should alerts go [Slack, Teams, email]?\n2. Which events do you want to hear about?\n3. Who should be mentioned when something breaks?\nBegin only after I answer.",
