    "description": "Moves repeated CI steps into reusable workflows and composite actions shared across repositories.",
    "rawContent": "I have the same pipeline copied across many repositories. Standardize it.\n \nSample workflows from different repos: {{SAMPLE_WORKFLOWS}}\nNumber of repos: {{REPO_COUNT}}\nWhat differs between repos: {{DIFFERENCES}}\n \nFind the common core, design a central repository with reusable workflows (inputs, secrets, outputs) and composite actions, versioned with tags. Show the caller workflow for a repo in 10 lines. Include a rollout plan (pilot repo, then batch) and how to roll back a bad shared change.\n \nOutput the structure as a tree, then the files.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Send me this numbered list of questions and wait:\n1. Paste 2 or 3 workflows from different repositories.\n2. How many repositories use this pattern?\n3. What changes from repo to repo [language, deploy target]?\nAfter I answer, begin the task.",
