    "title": "Database: Migration Step Inside the Pipeline",
    "description": "Adds safe database migration jobs to CI/CD with ordering, locks, and failure handling.",
    "rawContent": "Add database migrations to my deploy pipeline without causing outages.\n \nMigration tool: {{MIGRATION_TOOL}}\nDatabase and hosting: {{DATABASE_HOSTING}}\nCurrent deploy flow: {{DEPLOY_FLOW}}\n \nDesign: migration job placement relative to app deploy (and why), a dry-run check on pull requests against a throwaway database, a lock to prevent two migrations running at once, a pre-migration backup step, and what happens on failure. Cover backward-compatible migrations so old and new app versions both work during rollout.\n \nOutput the YAML and a rules list for developers writing migrations.\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me these questions in one message:\n1. Which migration tool do you use?\n2. Where is your database hosted?\n3. How does your app get deployed today?\nThen produce the result as soon as I reply.",
