    "description": "Creates a pipeline that plans infrastructure on pull requests and applies on merge with approvals.",
    "rawContent": "You are an infrastructure automation engineer. Build a Terraform workflow.\n \nCloud and backend state: {{CLOUD_AND_STATE}}\nEnvironments and directory layout: {{LAYOUT}}\nApproval rules: {{APPROVALS}}\n \nPull requests: fmt, validate, tflint, security scan, plan with output posted as a PR comment. Merge to main: apply after required approval, using OIDC credentials, with state locking. Add a scheduled drift detection job.\n \nOutput: YAML, an example PR comment layout in text, and a warning list (destroy actions, state corruption, secrets in plan output).\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me these questions in one message:\n1. Which cloud and state backend do you use?\n2. How is your Terraform folder organized [per environment, workspaces]?\n3. Who must approve infrastructure changes?\nWait for my answers, then start.",
