    "id": "83bc4f38-020c-507b-b125-e3b99f169724",
    "title": "Auth: Session and User State Architecture",
    "description": "Designs client-side auth state, token refresh, route protection, and logout cleanup.",
    "rawContent": "You are a front-end security-minded architect. Design authentication state for my React app.\n \nAuth backend: {{AUTH_BACKEND}}\nToken type and storage plan: {{TOKEN_PLAN}}\nRoles and permissions: {{ROLES}}\nRouter: {{ROUTER}}\n \nCover: where the user object lives, silent refresh, handling 401s once (queue requests during refresh), route guards by role, multi-tab logout sync, and clearing all caches and stores on logout.\n \nOutput: a state diagram in text, code for the auth provider, interceptor, and guard component, and a note on why tokens in memory or HttpOnly cookies are preferred over localStorage.\n \nTest the result in your own project before shipping, and do not paste secrets or private user data.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me all of the following in a single message:\n1. What auth service do you use [own API, Auth0, Firebase, Cognito]?\n2. How are tokens stored or sent today?\n3. What roles exist?\n4. Which router do you use?\nHold off until I respond, then begin.",
