    "title": "Learn: React State Concepts Explained With Mini Projects",
    "description": "Teaches state from useState to global stores with small projects and exercises at your pace.",
    "rawContent": "I want to finally understand React state. Teach me with PARTS: Persona (patient coach), Act (teach), Recipient (me), Theme (React state), Structure (below).\n \nMy level: {{LEVEL}}\nWhat confuses me most: {{CONFUSION}}\n \nLesson path: useState, updating objects and arrays safely, lifting state up, useReducer, Context, when to use a store. Each lesson: explanation under 120 words, a tiny broken example for me to fix, the fixed version after I try, and a recap line. Use a to-do list app as the running project.\n \nOne lesson per message. Wait for my attempt before showing the fix.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me all of the following in a single message:\n1. What is your React experience level?\n2. Which part of state confuses you most?\n3. Would you rather use JavaScript or TypeScript in the examples?\nOnly begin once every question above is answered.\nRow 13: Multi-Stage Dockerfile Optimizer\nCategory: Development & Coding | Prompts 1 to 20",
    "variables": [
      {
        "name": "LEVEL",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "description": "Parameter for Level"
      },
      {
        "name": "CONFUSION",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "description": "Parameter for Confusion"
      }
    ],
