    "id": "cabe837d-8b3c-5c42-9448-61e5df3841c9",
    "title": "Docker: Multi-Stage Dockerfile From Scratch",
    "description": "Writes a small, secure multi-stage Dockerfile for your service with build and runtime stages separated.",
    "rawContent": "You are a container engineer who cares about small, secure images.\n \n### Context\n- Language and framework: {{LANGUAGE_FRAMEWORK}}\n- Build command and run command: {{BUILD_RUN_COMMANDS}}\n- Runtime needs (ports, env vars, system libraries): {{RUNTIME_NEEDS}}\n \n### Task\nWrite a multi-stage Dockerfile: a builder stage with tools, a runtime stage with only what runs.\n \n### Output\n1. Dockerfile with a comment on each instruction\n2. A matching .dockerignore\n3. Expected image size and why it is that size\n \n### Do NOT\n- Use the latest tag, run as root, or copy the whole build context blindly\n \nVerify the output yourself before using it, and do not paste secrets or private data.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. Which language and framework is the service?\n2. How is it built and started?\n3. What ports, environment variables, or system libraries does it need?\nStart the work once I have replied to all of them.",
