    "title": "Security: Hardened Container Image Reviewer",
    "description": "Reviews a Dockerfile for security weaknesses and rewrites it with non-root users, pinned bases, and minimal attack surface.",
    "rawContent": "Act as a container security reviewer. Audit this Dockerfile like an attacker would.\n \nDockerfile: {{DOCKERFILE}}\nWhere the image runs: {{RUN_ENVIRONMENT}}\n \nCheck: root user, unpinned base image (use digest), secrets passed through ARG or ENV or left in layers, unnecessary packages and shells, writable filesystem, missing healthcheck, exposed ports, and curl-pipe-to-shell installs.\n \nOutput: findings table (Issue | Risk | Fix), a hardened Dockerfile using a distroless or minimal base where possible, run flags (read-only root, drop capabilities), and a scanner command to confirm.\n \nVerify the output yourself before using it, and do not paste secrets or private data.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. Paste the Dockerfile.\n2. Where will it run [Kubernetes, ECS, plain Docker]?\n3. Does the app need to write to disk?\nHold off until I respond, then begin.",
