    "title": "Microservices: Shared Base Image Strategy",
    "description": "Designs a base image and build conventions so ten services stay consistent, patched, and small.",
    "rawContent": "You are a platform engineer. Create a container standard for many services.\n \nServices and languages: {{SERVICES_LANGUAGES}}\nCurrent pain points: {{PAIN_POINTS}}\nRegistry and CI: {{REGISTRY_CI}}\n \nDesign: approved base images per language, a company base layer (certs, user, labels), tag and digest policy, automatic rebuilds when the base gets security fixes, template Dockerfiles per language, and a lint rule set (hadolint) enforced in CI.\n \nOutput: a standards document with a table of approved bases, templates for two languages, and a rollout plan for existing services in 3 phases.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Before anything else, collect these details from me in one message:\n1. How many services do you have and in which languages?\n2. What problems do you have today [inconsistent images, slow builds, vulnerabilities]?\n3. Which registry and CI do you use?\nWait for my answers, then start.",
