    "id": "41902392-b143-5786-990c-2685e11fdee9",
    "title": "Secrets: Safe Build Secrets and Config Handling",
    "description": "Handles private registry tokens and API keys in builds with BuildKit secrets and runtime injection.",
    "rawContent": "Show me how to use secrets in Docker builds without leaking them into image layers.\n \nWhat the build needs access to: {{BUILD_SECRETS}}\nWhat the app needs at runtime: {{RUNTIME_CONFIG}}\nOrchestrator: {{ORCHESTRATOR}}\n \nCover: why ARG and ENV leak, --mount=type=secret usage in RUN, SSH mounts for private git repos, multi-stage tricks (and why they are not enough alone), runtime injection through environment, mounted files, or a secrets manager, and how to scan an image for leaked secrets.\n \nOutput: before (leaky) and after (safe) Dockerfiles with a build command.\n \nVerify the output yourself before using it, and do not paste secrets or private data.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. What does the build need to access [private npm packages, private git, license keys]?\n2. How does the running app get its configuration today?\n3. Where do you run containers?\nOnly begin once every question above is answered.",
