    "description": "Builds a front-end bundle in one stage and serves it from a small Nginx or Caddy stage with proper caching headers.",
    "rawContent": "Write a Dockerfile and web server config to serve my front-end app.\n \nFramework and build command: {{FRAMEWORK_BUILD}}\nOutput folder: {{OUTPUT_DIR}}\nRouting type (SPA with client routes or multi-page): {{ROUTING}}\nAPI backend to proxy to: {{API_BACKEND}}\n \nStage 1 builds, stage 2 serves with nginx (unprivileged image). Include: SPA fallback to index.html, long cache for hashed assets, no-cache for index.html, gzip or brotli, security headers, runtime environment config without rebuilding, and a healthcheck.\n \nOutput the Dockerfile and nginx.conf.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Before anything else, collect these details from me in one message:\n1. Which framework builds your front end, and what is the build command?\n2. What folder holds the built files?\n3. Does it use client-side routing?\n4. Should it proxy API calls to a backend?\nBegin only after I answer.",
