    "description": "Builds reproducible ML images with CUDA, pinned libraries, and separate training and inference stages.",
    "rawContent": "As an MLOps engineer, create Dockerfiles for machine learning work.\n \nFramework (PyTorch, TensorFlow, other): {{ML_FRAMEWORK}}\nGPU type and CUDA version: {{GPU_CUDA}}\nTraining vs. inference needs: {{TRAINING_INFERENCE}}\nModel size and where weights are stored: {{MODEL_INFO}}\n \nDeliver a training stage image and a slim inference stage image from one multi-stage file. Pin library versions and CUDA compatibility, avoid baking large model weights into layers (download at start or mount), and keep image size reasonable. Add notes on NVIDIA container toolkit and driver compatibility.\n \nOutput: Dockerfile, run commands, and a size comparison table.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. Which ML framework and version?\n2. What GPU and CUDA version are available?\n3. Do you need training, inference, or both?\n4. How large are the model files?\nAfter I answer, begin the task.",
