    "description": "Builds a pipeline stage that lints, builds, scans, signs, and pushes images with fail rules.",
    "rawContent": "Create the image supply-chain stage for my CI. Role: DevSecOps engineer.\n \nCI platform: {{CI_PLATFORM}}\nRegistry: {{REGISTRY}}\nSeverity policy: {{SEVERITY_POLICY}}\n \nSteps: hadolint on the Dockerfile, build with BuildKit and cache, Trivy or Grype scan failing on the chosen severity with an allow-list file for accepted risks (each with expiry), generate an SBOM, sign with cosign keyless, push only from main, and verify the signature at deploy time.\n \nOutput: pipeline YAML and a short policy on how exceptions are approved.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Before anything else, collect these details from me in one message:\n1. Which CI platform do you use?\n2. Which registry holds the images?\n3. What severity of vulnerability should block a release?\nThen produce the result as soon as I reply.",
