    "description": "Aligns Dockerfile choices with Kubernetes resources, probes, signals, and security context.",
    "rawContent": "Review my Dockerfile together with my Kubernetes deployment so they agree.\n \nDockerfile: {{DOCKERFILE}}\nKubernetes manifest: {{K8S_MANIFEST}}\nObserved problems: {{PROBLEMS}}\n \nCheck: user ID vs. runAsNonRoot, read-only root filesystem with writable tmp volumes, memory limits vs. runtime memory settings (JVM, Node heap), liveness and readiness probes vs. startup time, graceful shutdown with SIGTERM and terminationGracePeriodSeconds, and image pull policy.\n \nOutput: mismatch table and corrected snippets for both files.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. Paste the Dockerfile.\n2. Paste the Deployment manifest.\n3. What problems do you see [restarts, OOM kills, slow rollouts]?\nStart the work once I have replied to all of them.",
