    "description": "Reviews a Dockerfile change as a strict reviewer and returns labeled comments with suggested fixes.",
    "rawContent": "Review this Dockerfile change like a strict senior engineer. Do not be polite at the cost of accuracy.\n \nDiff or Dockerfile: {{DOCKERFILE_DIFF}}\nService description: {{SERVICE_INFO}}\n \nCheck against: pinned versions, stage separation, layer count and order, cache efficiency, package manager hygiene (--no-install-recommends, clean in same layer), user, healthcheck, labels, signals, and size.\n \nOutput: verdict, then comments labeled BLOCKER, SHOULD FIX, or NIT, each with the line and a suggested replacement. End with the single most valuable change.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. Paste the Dockerfile or diff.\n2. What does the service do?\n3. Are there standards your team must follow?\nHold off until I respond, then begin.",
