    "id": "4eb49eb8-0755-537e-a701-1d82b3bac678",
    "title": "Patterns: Common Node.js Leak Cause Detector",
    "description": "Scans your code for the usual leak culprits like unbounded caches, listeners, closures, and timers.",
    "rawContent": "Review my code only for memory leak patterns.\n \nCode: {{PASTED_CODE}}\nWhat the service does: {{SERVICE_PURPOSE}}\n \nCheck for: Maps, Sets, or arrays that only grow, caches without size limits or TTL, event listeners added per request and never removed, setInterval without clearInterval, closures holding large objects, global variables, unclosed streams or database connections, promises that never settle, and request objects stored in module scope.\n \nOutput: findings with line numbers, memory growth estimate per request if possible, and the fixed code. Mark each finding Confirmed (clearly leaks) or Suspected (depends on usage).\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me these questions in one message:\n1. Paste the code you suspect.\n2. What does the service do and how many requests per minute does it handle?\n3. Are there long-lived modules, caches, or background jobs?\nWait for my answers, then start.",
