    "description": "Investigates leaks outside the JS heap from native modules, buffers, and file descriptors.",
    "rawContent": "My RSS keeps growing but the V8 heap looks flat. Help me investigate non-heap memory.\n \nProcess metrics over time (rss, heapUsed, external, arrayBuffers): {{METRICS}}\nNative modules in use (sharp, bcrypt, canvas, database drivers): {{NATIVE_MODULES}}\nOS and container info: {{OS_INFO}}\n \nWork in stages: (1) read the metrics to say which memory class grows, (2) list suspect modules and known leak patterns, (3) give commands for the OS (pmap, /proc/PID/smaps, lsof counts, jemalloc profiling), (4) suggest isolation tests (disable one module at a time), (5) mention glibc fragmentation and MALLOC_ARENA_MAX as a possible cause.\n \nOutput: ranked hypotheses with the test for each.\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me these questions in one message:\n1. Paste memory metrics over time [rss, heapUsed, external].\n2. Which native or compiled packages do you use?\n3. Which OS or container base image is in use?\nWait for my answers, then start.",
