    "description": "Gives an on-call runbook for handling a suspected memory leak in production with minimal risk.",
    "rawContent": "Write an on-call runbook for when memory alarms fire on a Node service. Tone: calm, short steps.\n \nService and hosting: {{SERVICE_HOSTING}}\nCurrent restart and scaling setup: {{SCALING_SETUP}}\nTolerance for downtime: {{DOWNTIME_TOLERANCE}}\n \nSections: first 5 minutes (confirm it is memory, check recent deploys), mitigation (rolling restart, scale out, traffic shift, memory-based auto restart as a stopgap), evidence capture before restarting (heap snapshot, metrics export, logs), communication template, and the follow-up ticket template.\n \nOutput as a checklist with commands. Warn about snapshot pauses and sensitive data inside heap dumps.\n \nVerify the output yourself before using it, and do not paste secrets or private data.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Send me this numbered list of questions and wait:\n1. Where does the service run?\n2. How does it restart and scale today?\n3. How much downtime or slowness is acceptable during investigation?\nOnly begin once every question above is answered.",
