    "description": "Reviews a leak fix and creates a memory regression test to prevent the bug from returning.",
    "rawContent": "Act as a skeptical reviewer. Does this change really fix the leak?\n \nOriginal code: {{ORIGINAL_CODE}}\nPatched code: {{PATCHED_CODE}}\nBefore and after memory measurements: {{MEASUREMENTS}}\n \nCheck whether the patch removes the retention path or only slows growth, whether any other path holds the same objects, and whether measurements were taken with forced GC and long enough.\n \nThen write an automated regression test: run the operation N times, force GC with --expose-gc, assert heapUsed growth stays under a threshold with tolerance, and a WeakRef-based test proving objects are collectable.\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me these questions in one message:\n1. Paste the original and patched code.\n2. Share memory measurements before and after.\n3. Which test runner do you use?\nBegin only after I answer.",
