    "id": "a5d79d20-1d69-59ae-8f3c-f233059ca817",
    "title": "Docker: Containerized Node Memory Limits and OOM Kill Debugger",
    "description": "Explains why Node containers get OOM-killed and aligns heap settings, limits, and requests.",
    "rawContent": "Debug why my Node container keeps getting killed.\n \nExit code and event details: {{KILL_DETAILS}}\nContainer memory limit and request: {{LIMITS}}\nNode flags and version: {{NODE_FLAGS}}\nMemory graph description: {{MEMORY_PATTERN}}\n \nExplain exit code 137 and the difference between a V8 heap out-of-memory crash and a kernel OOM kill. Determine which one I have from the details. Calculate a safe --max-old-space-size (roughly 70 to 75 percent of the limit, show the arithmetic) and explain what else uses memory (buffers, native code, worker threads).\n \nOutput: diagnosis, corrected settings, and a one-line command to check cgroup memory inside the container.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Send me this numbered list of questions and wait:\n1. What exit code or event do you see [137, OOMKilled, heap out of memory]?\n2. What are the container memory limit and request?\n3. Which Node version and flags are set?\nHold off until I respond, then begin.\nRow 15: Feature Scaffolding Generator\nCategory: Development & Coding | Prompts 1 to 20",
    "variables": [
      {
        "name": "KILL_DETAILS",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "description": "Parameter for Kill Details"
      },
      {
        "name": "LIMITS",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "description": "Parameter for Limits"
      },
      {
        "name": "NODE_FLAGS",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "description": "Parameter for Node Flags"
      },
      {
        "name": "MEMORY_PATTERN",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "description": "Parameter for Memory Pattern"
      }
    ],
