    "description": "Creates the skeleton for browser extensions, editor plugins, or CMS plugins with manifests and permissions.",
    "rawContent": "Help me start a plugin. I know the idea but not the required file structure.\n \nPlatform: {{PLATFORM}}\nWhat the plugin does: {{PLUGIN_PURPOSE}}\nPermissions or APIs it needs: {{PERMISSIONS}}\n \nGenerate every required file: manifest or package config with the minimum permissions (and why each is needed), entry points, a sample feature that works, a settings page if relevant, build and run instructions, and a debug how-to for this platform.\n \nTell me to check the platform's current documentation because manifest rules change often.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Interview me first with these questions, all in one message:\n1. Which platform is it for [Chrome, VS Code, WordPress, Figma, Shopify]?\n2. What should the plugin do?\n3. What data or browser features does it need to access?\nThen produce the result as soon as I reply.",
