    "title": "Data: Pipeline Job Scaffold for ETL and Scheduled Tasks",
    "description": "Generates a data pipeline job skeleton with config, retries, idempotency, logging, and data tests.",
    "rawContent": "As a data engineer, create a pipeline job template.\n \nSource and destination: {{SOURCE_DESTINATION}}\nSchedule and volume: {{SCHEDULE_VOLUME}}\nLanguage and orchestrator: {{LANGUAGE_ORCHESTRATOR}}\n \nGenerate: extract, transform, and load modules as separate functions, config file with environment overrides, idempotent writes (upsert or partition overwrite), retry with backoff, structured logs with run IDs, data quality checks (row counts, nulls, duplicates), a backfill option by date range, unit tests with sample data, and orchestrator definition.\n \nOutput the tree and files. Add a runbook paragraph for failures.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me all of the following in a single message:\n1. Where does the data come from and where does it go?\n2. How often does it run and how much data is there?\n3. Which language and scheduler do you use [Airflow, cron, Prefect]?\nStart the work once I have replied to all of them.",
