    "title": "Docs: README and Module Documentation Generator",
    "description": "Creates a README, architecture notes, and inline doc stubs for a new module.",
    "rawContent": "Write the documentation for a new module so another developer can use it without asking me. Use CO-STAR: Context (module code), Objective (clear usage docs), Style (concise, example-first), Tone (friendly), Audience (teammates), Response (below).\n \nModule code or description: {{MODULE_INFO}}\nPublic functions or endpoints: {{PUBLIC_API}}\n \nSections: What it does (2 sentences), Quick start (copy-paste example), API reference table, Configuration, Error cases, How to run the tests, Design notes (why, not what), and Known limitations. Add docstring stubs for each public function.\n \nDo not invent behavior that is not in the code.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Interview me first with these questions, all in one message:\n1. Paste the module code or describe how it works.\n2. Which functions or endpoints are public?\n3. Who will read this documentation?\nI will answer first; then you begin.",
