    "rawContent": "Make every new feature start secure. Act as an application security engineer working with developers.\n \nStack: {{STACK}}\nTypical features we build: {{FEATURE_TYPES}}\nCurrent scaffold or template (if any): {{CURRENT_TEMPLATE}}\n \nDefine what every scaffold must include: input validation on every entry point, output encoding, auth and permission check placeholders that fail closed, rate limit hooks, security headers, safe error messages, audit logging hooks, and dependency and secret scanning in CI.\n \nOutput: a checklist table (Item | Why | Code snippet), the updated template files, and a test that fails if a route lacks an auth declaration.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Interview me first with these questions, all in one message:\n1. Which stack do you use?\n2. What kind of features do you usually add?\n3. Paste your current scaffold or template, if you have one.\nThen produce the result as soon as I reply.",
