    "title": "Learn: Project Structure Best Practices Explained",
    "description": "Teaches how to organize folders and modules in your language with examples and exercises.",
    "rawContent": "Teach me how to organize a project so it stays tidy as it grows. Use PARTS: Persona (friendly mentor), Act (teach), Recipient (me), Theme (project structure), Structure (below).\n \nMy language and framework: {{STACK}}\nProject size today: {{PROJECT_SIZE}}\n \nLessons: why structure matters, organize by type vs. by feature, naming rules, where shared code lives, how to keep dependencies flowing one way, and when to split a module. For each: a bad tree, a better tree, and a 2-sentence reason. After each lesson give me a messy tree and ask me to reorganize it. Wait for my answer.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Interview me first with these questions, all in one message:\n1. Which language and framework are you learning?\n2. How big is your project right now?\n3. What is the biggest mess in it today?\nWait for my answers, then start.\nRow 16: Strict Pull Request Reviewer\nCategory: Development & Coding | Prompts 1 to 20",
    "variables": [
      {
        "name": "STACK",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "description": "Parameter for Stack"
      },
      {
        "name": "PROJECT_SIZE",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "description": "Parameter for Project Size"
      }
    ],
