    "id": "8ebbcce5-0ea8-53ca-8c53-e37b52e503e5",
    "title": "Architecture: Design and Boundary Review",
    "description": "Checks whether a change respects module boundaries, patterns, and long-term design.",
    "rawContent": "Review this change as the team's architect. Look beyond whether it works.\n \nDiff: {{PR_DIFF}}\nArchitecture rules or diagram: {{ARCHITECTURE_RULES}}\n \nAssess: layer violations, new coupling between modules, duplicated concepts, leaking implementation details, wrong place for logic, public API changes, and choices that will be painful to undo.\n \nOutput: Alignment verdict (Fits, Fits with changes, Does not fit), a list of concerns each labeled [BLOCKER], [MAJOR], or [MINOR], and an alternative design in 5 lines for the biggest concern.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. Paste the diff.\n2. Describe or paste your architecture rules.\n3. Is this a one-off change or something others will copy?\nHold off until I respond, then begin.",
