    "description": "Reviews database migrations and queries in a pull request for locking, data loss, and index issues.",
    "rawContent": "Review the database changes in this pull request as a cautious DBA.\n \nMigration files and queries: {{DB_CHANGES}}\nTable sizes and database engine: {{TABLE_SIZES_ENGINE}}\nHow the app is deployed: {{DEPLOY_METHOD}}\n \nChecks: locks on big tables, irreversible steps, data loss, defaults rewriting rows, missing down migration, new foreign keys without indexes, queries that cannot use indexes, ordering with the app deploy, and backward compatibility during rolling deploys.\n \nOutput: verdict, issues labeled [BLOCKER], [MAJOR], [MINOR], and a safer rewrite of the riskiest step.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. Paste the migration and changed queries.\n2. Which database and how large are the affected tables?\n3. Do old and new app versions run at the same time during deploy?\nAfter I answer, begin the task.",
