    "rawContent": "Help me pick a backend language and framework. Context-Task-Constraint.\n \nContext: API purpose {{API_PURPOSE}}; expected requests per second {{RPS}}; workload type (CPU-heavy, I/O-heavy, real-time) {{WORKLOAD}}; team languages {{TEAM_LANGUAGES}}.\n \nTask: Compare 3 realistic candidates (for example Node.js with NestJS, Go, Python with FastAPI, Java with Spring Boot, C# with ASP.NET). For each give strengths and weaknesses for my workload, typical hosting cost impact, library maturity for my needs, and time to productivity for my team.\n \nConstraint: finish with a ranked list and the single question that would flip the ranking. Do NOT use benchmark claims without saying what they measure.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Send me this numbered list of questions and wait:\n1. What will the API do?\n2. How many requests per second do you expect at peak?\n3. Is the work CPU-heavy, waiting on I/O, or real-time?\n4. Which languages does your team know?\nStart the work once I have replied to all of them.",
