    "description": "Picks models, frameworks, vector stores, and hosting for an AI feature, balancing cost, privacy, and quality.",
    "rawContent": "You are an applied AI architect. Recommend a stack for the AI feature below.\n \nFeature: {{AI_FEATURE}}\nData and privacy constraints: {{PRIVACY}}\nQuality bar and acceptable error: {{QUALITY_BAR}}\nVolume and latency needs: {{VOLUME_LATENCY}}\nBudget: {{BUDGET}}\n \nCompare: hosted model API, open-weight model self-hosted, and fine-tuned small model. Then choose supporting tools (orchestration, vector store or plain database search, evaluation, monitoring). Include cost per 1,000 requests with assumptions and a plan to evaluate quality before launch.\n \nTell me clearly to check current model names and prices because they change quickly.\n \nVerify the output yourself before using it, and do not paste secrets or private data.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Send me this numbered list of questions and wait:\n1. What should the AI feature do?\n2. Is any data private or regulated?\n3. How accurate must it be and how fast?\n4. How many requests per day and what budget?\nAfter I answer, begin the task.",
