    "title": "Present: Stack Recommendation Pitch for Non-Technical Stakeholders",
    "description": "Turns a technical stack decision into a clear business pitch with risks, costs, and timeline.",
    "rawContent": "Explain our technology decision so a non-technical leader can approve it. Use PARTS: Persona (trusted technical advisor), Act (explain and persuade honestly), Recipient ({{AUDIENCE}}), Theme (our stack choice), Structure (below).\n \nOur recommendation: {{RECOMMENDATION}}\nKey reasons: {{KEY_REASONS}}\nCosts and timeline: {{COSTS_TIMELINE}}\nMain risks: {{RISKS}}\n \nStructure: the decision in one sentence, why it matters to the business, what it costs, what could go wrong and how we handle it, what we need approved, and a slide-by-slide outline (6 slides). No jargon; if a technical word is unavoidable, explain it in brackets.\n \nDo not start the task yet. First ask me these questions in one message:\n1. What are you recommending?\n2. What are the main reasons for it?\n3. What are the costs and the timeline?\n4. Who is the audience [CEO, finance, board, client]?\nThen produce the result as soon as I reply.\nRow 18: CLI Tool Builder\nCategory: Development & Coding | Prompts 1 to 20",
