    "description": "Designs subcommands, flags, and defaults for a CLI so it feels natural and stays consistent.",
    "rawContent": "Help me design the command-line interface of my tool before I write any code. Think like the designer of git or docker.\n \nTool purpose: {{TOOL_PURPOSE}}\nMain user actions: {{USER_ACTIONS}}\nWho uses it [developers, admins, data analysts]: {{USERS}}\nShared options needed everywhere (verbose, config file, output format): {{GLOBAL_OPTIONS}}\n \nStage 1: list nouns and verbs. Stage 2: propose the command tree. Stage 3: define every flag (long and short name, type, default, required or not). Stage 4: show 6 realistic example invocations. Stage 5: show the --help output for the top level and one subcommand.\n \nFollow the rule: one way to do each thing, flags have the same meaning everywhere.\n \nOutput as a command tree, a flag table, and the help text.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Interview me first with these questions, all in one message:\n1. What does the tool do?\n2. List the main actions users will take.\n3. Who will use it?\n4. Are there options that should work on every command?\n5. Should it read a config file or environment variables as well?\nBegin only after I answer.",
