    "title": "jQuery: Codebase Audit and Migration Roadmap",
    "description": "Audits how jQuery is used across your project and produces a phased plan to replace it with vanilla JavaScript.",
    "rawContent": "You are a front-end modernization lead planning the removal of jQuery from a production site.\n \n### Context\n- jQuery version and plugins: {{JQUERY_VERSION_PLUGINS}}\n- Size of the codebase (files, pages): {{CODEBASE_SIZE}}\n- Browser support required: {{BROWSER_SUPPORT}}\n- Sample of typical jQuery code: {{SAMPLE_CODE}}\n \n### Task\nBuild a phased roadmap. Work in stages: (1) inventory usage by category (selectors, DOM changes, events, AJAX, animation, utilities, plugins), (2) rate migration difficulty per category, (3) order the work from lowest to highest risk, (4) define a test checkpoint after each phase.\n \n### Output\nInventory table, a 4-phase roadmap with effort in days, and a list of plugins that need replacement with named alternatives.\n \n### Do NOT\n- Suggest a big-bang rewrite\n \nReview the roadmap with your team before starting.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. Which jQuery version and which plugins do you use?\n2. How many files or pages use jQuery?\n3. Which browsers must still work [IE11, latest only]?\n4. Paste a few typical snippets.\n5. How many developers and how much time can you spend?\nHold off until I respond, then begin.",
    "variables": [
      {
        "name": "JQUERY_VERSION_PLUGINS",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "description": "Parameter for Jquery Version Plugins"
      },
      {
        "name": "CODEBASE_SIZE",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "description": "Parameter for Codebase Size"
      },
      {
        "name": "BROWSER_SUPPORT",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "description": "Parameter for Browser Support"
      },
      {
        "name": "SAMPLE_CODE",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "description": "Parameter for Sample Code"
      }
    ],
