    "description": "Rewrites jQuery AJAX calls with fetch or async/await, including error handling, JSON, forms, and timeouts.",
    "rawContent": "Can you rewrite my $.ajax, $.get, and $.post calls using fetch with async/await?\n \nCalls to convert: {{AJAX_CODE}}\nServer expectations (JSON, form data, CSRF token, cookies): {{SERVER_NOTES}}\n \nRemember the traps: fetch does not reject on HTTP errors (check response.ok), cookies need credentials settings, no built-in timeout (use AbortSignal.timeout), and form encoding differs. Create one small reusable request helper instead of repeating code.\n \nOutput: helper function, each call converted, and a table of behavior differences.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Before anything else, collect these details from me in one message:\n1. Paste the AJAX code.\n2. What does the server expect and return?\n3. Does it use cookies or a CSRF token?\nBegin only after I answer.",
