    "description": "Replaces .animate(), .fadeIn(), and .slideToggle() with CSS transitions and the Web Animations API.",
    "rawContent": "As a front-end animation specialist, replace my jQuery animations.\n \nAnimation code: {{ANIMATION_CODE}}\nElements involved and their CSS: {{ELEMENTS_CSS}}\n \nFor each animation decide between a CSS transition, CSS keyframes, or element.animate(). Animate transform and opacity instead of height or top where possible, handle height-auto slides with a safe technique, support prefers-reduced-motion, and keep callbacks working through the finished promise or transitionend.\n \nOutput: converted code, CSS, and a note on performance gains.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Before anything else, collect these details from me in one message:\n1. Paste the jQuery animation code.\n2. Paste the related HTML and CSS.\n3. Should animations be disabled for users who prefer reduced motion?\nThen produce the result as soon as I reply.",
