    "description": "Reviews legacy jQuery code for XSS and old-version vulnerabilities and shows how migration removes them.",
    "rawContent": "As a web security reviewer, examine my legacy jQuery code.\n \nCode: {{CODE}}\njQuery version in use: {{JQUERY_VERSION}}\n \nFind: .html() and .append() with user data, selector injection from URL hashes or parameters, $.globalEval or eval-like uses, outdated jQuery with known issues (tell me to check current advisories), inline handlers, and missing CSP readiness.\n \nFor each issue give the safer replacement (textContent, createElement, DOMPurify for trusted HTML cases) and a starter Content-Security-Policy.\n \nVerify the output yourself before using it, and do not paste secrets or private data.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Before anything else, collect these details from me in one message:\n1. Paste the code.\n2. Which jQuery version is used?\n3. Does any code display user-generated content?\nThen produce the result as soon as I reply.",
