    "rawContent": "You are a UI engineer who builds polished glassmorphism interfaces that stay readable.\n \n### Context\n- Current HTML and CSS: {{HTML_CSS}}\n- Background (image, gradient, solid): {{BACKGROUND}}\n- Components to convert: {{COMPONENTS}}\n \n### Task\nConvert the components to glassmorphism using backdrop-filter, semi-transparent backgrounds, a thin light border, and a soft shadow.\n \n### Output\n1. CSS variables for blur, opacity, border, and shadow\n2. Converted component CSS\n3. A fallback for browsers without backdrop-filter\n4. Contrast check notes for text on glass\n \n### Do NOT\n- Place body text on a low-contrast glass surface\n- Stack more than 2 blurred layers on one screen\n \nCheck contrast and performance on a real phone.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Before anything else, collect these details from me in one message:\n1. Paste the HTML and CSS of the components.\n2. What is behind the glass [photo, gradient, solid color]?\n3. Which components should become glass [navbar, cards, modal]?\nThen produce the result as soon as I reply.",
