    "title": "Learn: Glassmorphism CSS Step by Step",
    "description": "Teaches blur, transparency, borders, and layering through small exercises you can run in the browser.",
    "rawContent": "Teach me glassmorphism in CSS by making me build it. Use PARTS: Persona (friendly CSS coach), Act (teach by exercises), Recipient (me), Theme (glass UI), Structure (below).\n \nMy CSS level: {{LEVEL}}\n \nSteps: (1) a colorful background, (2) a plain card, (3) add transparency with rgba, (4) add backdrop-filter blur, (5) add a light border, (6) add a soft shadow, (7) fix readability. At each step give 5 lines of code and one thing to experiment with, and ask me what I see. Wait for my reply.\n \nDo not start the task yet. I will need the answers to these first, so ask them together:\n1. What is your CSS level?\n2. Do you use CodePen, a local editor, or something else?\nHold off until I respond, then begin.\nRow 23: Flawless Dark Mode Refactor\nCategory: Web Design & UI/UX | Prompts 1 to 20",
