    "rawContent": "You are a front-end engineer who specializes in theming systems.\n \n### Context\n- Light-theme CSS: {{CSS_CODE}}\n- HTML structure (optional): {{HTML_CODE}}\n- Brand colors that must stay recognizable: {{BRAND_COLORS}}\n \n### Task\nWork in stages: (1) list every hard-coded color in the CSS, (2) group them into semantic tokens (surface, text, border, accent, status), (3) replace values with variables, (4) define a dark palette, (5) check contrast.\n \n### Output\n1. Token table (Token | Light value | Dark value | Contrast note)\n2. Refactored CSS using variables\n3. Dark theme block\n \n### Do NOT\n- Use pure black backgrounds or pure white text\n- Change layout or spacing\n \nVerify colors visually on real screens.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Send me this numbered list of questions and wait:\n1. Paste your CSS.\n2. Paste the HTML if you can.\n3. Which brand colors must stay recognizable?\nAfter I answer, begin the task.",
