    "title": "Motion: Safe Animation and Media Accessibility",
    "description": "Controls motion, autoplay, flashing, and time limits so content is safe for vestibular and seizure conditions.",
    "rawContent": "Audit my motion and media for accessibility risks.\n \nAnimations, carousels, videos, and audio on the page: {{MOTION_MEDIA}}\nCSS and JavaScript: {{CODE}}\n \nCheck: prefers-reduced-motion support, pause or stop control for anything moving over 5 seconds, no content flashing more than 3 times per second, autoplay with sound, captions and transcripts for video, audio descriptions where needed, and time limits that users can extend.\n \nOutput: issue table with the success criterion and fixes in code. Include a safe default for each animation.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Interview me first with these questions, all in one message:\n1. List the animations and media on the page.\n2. Paste the related CSS and JavaScript.\n3. Is there any video or audio content?\nBegin only after I answer.",
