    "description": "Guides you to fix PDFs and Office documents with tags, reading order, and alt text.",
    "rawContent": "Help me make my documents accessible before publishing.\n \nDocument type and tool used to create it: {{DOCUMENT_TYPE_TOOL}}\nContent features (tables, images, forms, columns): {{CONTENT_FEATURES}}\n \nGive a step-by-step remediation checklist for the source tool first (headings, lists, alt text, table headers, document language), the export settings that create a tagged PDF, then checks in a PDF reader: tags tree, reading order, form field labels, bookmarks, and title. Include how to test with a screen reader.\n \nOutput: checklist grouped by stage.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Interview me first with these questions, all in one message:\n1. Which program creates the document [Word, InDesign, Google Docs]?\n2. Does it include tables, images, or forms?\nI will answer first; then you begin.",
