    "description": "Plans how complex dashboard panels reorder, collapse, or scroll on smaller screens.",
    "rawContent": "Dashboards break on phones. Design the reflow plan.\n \nDesktop panel layout: {{DESKTOP_LAYOUT}}\nMost important phone tasks: {{PHONE_TASKS}}\nPanel types (charts, tables, maps, KPIs): {{PANEL_TYPES}}\n \nFor each breakpoint decide: panel order, which panels collapse into tabs or accordions, which tables become cards or horizontally scroll inside a container, which charts simplify, and which move behind a 'more' action. Use CSS Grid with auto-fit and minmax plus container queries so panels respond to their own width.\n \nOutput: reflow table (Panel | Desktop | Tablet | Phone) and CSS.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Before anything else, collect these details from me in one message:\n1. Describe or paste your desktop layout.\n2. What do people need to do on a phone?\n3. What types of panels are included?\nI will answer first; then you begin.",
