    "description": "Audits glass interfaces for unreadable text and fixes contrast with scrims, text shadows, and adaptive tints.",
    "rawContent": "Glass UIs often fail accessibility. Check mine.\n \nProcess: list each text element over glass; estimate worst-case contrast against the lightest and darkest parts of the background; flag anything below WCAG AA (4.5:1 body, 3:1 large); propose fixes (darker tint layer, subtle scrim, heavier font weight, text-shadow) with exact CSS; add a prefers-contrast and prefers-reduced-transparency fallback.\n \nBe honest when you cannot compute contrast exactly; show your estimate method.\n \nAsk me to paste the code and describe or list the backgrounds that appear behind the glass.",
