    "description": "Audits a neumorphic design for low contrast and unclear boundaries, and adds fixes that keep the soft look.",
    "rawContent": "Soft UI is famous for poor accessibility. Audit mine honestly.\n \nCheck: text contrast (4.5:1), component boundary contrast (3:1 under WCAG 1.4.11), focus indicators, disabled vs enabled distinction, and whether users can tell what is clickable.\n \nOutput: Problem | Evidence | Fix, then a rewritten CSS snippet showing the fix with a subtle border, stronger text color, and clearer states.\n \nDo NOT say the design is accessible if you cannot verify.\n \nAsk me to paste the CSS and describe the main screens.",
