    "description": "Teaches how to name and lock static objects so simulation prompts do not warp the surroundings.",
    "rawContent": "Teach and apply the geometry lock technique.\n \nSteps: list fixed objects, describe each with material and exact position, add an explicit locked-elements sentence, keep the camera static or on a defined path, put motion words only on the fluid, and avoid verbs that apply to fixed objects.\n \nThen rewrite my prompt with the lock applied and highlight what changed.\n \nAsk me to paste the prompt and tell me which objects must stay rigid.",
