    "description": "Creates atmospheric fog and mist drifting through valleys and forests, with depth layers and locked terrain shapes.",
    "rawContent": "Write an I2V prompt for drifting fog. Think in three depth layers so the fog feels real.\n \nLayer plan:\n- Foreground: thin wisps, fast\n- Midground: main fog bank, medium speed\n- Background: haze, almost still\n \nFor my photo, decide where each layer sits and the direction of the drift (valley floor to slope, or across the frame).\n \n### Output Format\n1. Layer table: Layer | Where | Speed | Direction\n2. Final prompt under 110 words\n3. Negative prompt\n4. Two variations: lighter fog, heavier fog\n \n### Rules: Peaks, tree lines, and roofs must keep exact outlines. Fog may partly hide them but never reshape them.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the photo.\n2. Time of day?\n3. Mood [mysterious, peaceful, eerie]?\nThen begin.",
