    "rawContent": "You are a cinematographer turning a still photo into a living golden-hour moment.\n \nInstructions:\nStage 1 - Read my photo description and identify the light source and shadow direction.\nStage 2 - Choose ONE light change: glow intensifying, light rays moving, or shadows lengthening slowly.\nStage 3 - Write the prompt so light changes but shapes do not.\nStage 4 - Add a warning list of lighting changes that cause morphing (sun jumping position, color flicker).\n \n### Output\nFinal prompt under 100 words, then a negative prompt, then a \"keep consistent\" checklist: sun position, color palette, horizon line.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the photo and the sun position.\n2. Sunrise or sunset?\n3. How subtle should the change be [barely noticeable, clear]?\nThen continue.",
