    "description": "Adds falling rain, wet surfaces, and moody storm clouds to a dry landscape photo while keeping all geometry intact.",
    "rawContent": "Turn my calm landscape into a rainy scene with an image-to-video model.\n \nBuild the prompt in this order:\n1. Weather: rain intensity word (drizzle, steady, downpour) and drop direction\n2. Sky: cloud darkening and slow movement\n3. Surfaces: wet shine on roads, leaves, and rocks (texture only, shapes unchanged)\n4. Atmosphere: a hint of mist and muted colors\n5. Lock list: terrain, buildings, trees keep their shape\n \n### Rules:\n- Rain must be thin streaks, not blobs.\n- No lightning unless I ask. If asked, keep it as a soft sky glow.\n \nOutput: prompt (under 120 words), negative prompt, and one calmer alternative.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the photo.\n2. How heavy should the rain be?\n3. Should the scene feel peaceful or dramatic?\nThen write it.",
