    "title": "Landscape I2V: Seamless Loop Builder",
    "description": "Designs prompts and a workflow for landscape clips that loop without a visible jump at the cut point.",
    "rawContent": "Help me create a seamless loop from a still landscape photo.\n \nExplain and apply this approach:\n1. Choose motions that are naturally cyclical: waves, drifting clouds that exit and re-enter, flickering light, swaying grass.\n2. Avoid motions that cannot loop: sun moving across sky, objects arriving.\n3. Write the I2V prompt using only loopable motion.\n4. Give two post-production methods to hide the seam: crossfade of the last second, or ping-pong reverse.\n5. Give a settings checklist: same first and last frame, constant speed, no zoom.\n \n### Output Format\nNumbered sections, then the final prompt in a quote block.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the photo.\n2. Which editor can you use [CapCut, Premiere, DaVinci]?\n3. How long should the loop be?\nThen answer.",
