    "description": "Keeps castles, churches, villages, and bridges perfectly rigid while the surrounding sky, water, or mist moves.",
    "rawContent": "Buildings in my photo keep bending when I animate it. Write a prompt that treats them as rigid.\n \nMethod:\n1. Name each structure in the photo and describe its shape in one phrase (a stone tower with a conical roof).\n2. State they are \"static, rigid, with straight edges and unchanged windows\".\n3. Pick one animated element (sky, mist, water) and describe it far away from the buildings in the prompt text.\n4. Add negative phrases: bending walls, wavy lines, melting roofs, shifting windows.\n5. Recommend a very low motion strength and a short clip.\n \n### Output\nPrompt under 110 words, negative prompt, and two settings tips.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. List the buildings in the photo.\n2. What should move?\n3. Which model?\nBegin after I answer.",
