    "description": "Animates the northern lights, star twinkle, and moving night clouds over a locked silhouette landscape.",
    "rawContent": "Animate a night sky photo with image-to-video.\n \nWrite the prompt with these parts:\n- Aurora: ribbon shape, color range, slow wave motion\n- Stars: tiny twinkle only, positions fixed\n- Clouds: optional thin passing wisps\n- Foreground silhouettes (mountains, trees, cabin): locked, dark, unchanged\n- Lighting: foreground gets faint glow from the aurora only\n \nAlso add a long-exposure feel instruction so motion looks smooth, not jumpy.\n \n### Output\nPrompt under 120 words, negative prompt (no shooting stars, no moving constellations, no brightening of the foreground), and a note on speeding up the aurora to look like a time-lapse.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the photo.\n2. Which colors for the aurora?\n3. Model and length?\nThen write it.",
