    "description": "Animates a vehicle along a winding mountain road with consistent scenery and believable parallax and curves.",
    "rawContent": "A winding road gives too many ways for the model to go wrong. Make a prompt that stays safe.\n \nStages:\n1. Define one simple path: the car moves forward along a gentle curve, away from the camera or alongside it.\n2. Lock the vehicle details and name the road edges, guardrails, and mountains as stable structures.\n3. Choose background motion: foreground trees streak, distant peaks barely move (parallax).\n4. Set camera: a steady helicopter-style follow shot or a fixed roadside pan.\n5. Write the prompt and negative prompt.\n \n### Rules:\n- Road width and lane markings remain consistent.\n- No sudden turns or elevation jumps.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the photo.\n2. Should the car approach, leave, or pass by?\n3. Model and clip length?\nThen write.",
