    "title": "Vehicle I2V: Motion Blur Control Language",
    "description": "Teaches how to describe shutter speed, panning blur, and background streaks so the vehicle stays crisp and the world streaks.",
    "rawContent": "Teach me to control motion blur with words.\n \nCover:\n1. Photography ideas in simple terms: shutter speed, panning, subject sharpness.\n2. A phrase library with three levels: light, medium, extreme blur. Give 5 phrases for each level.\n3. How to say \"subject sharp, background streaked\" without the model blurring the vehicle.\n4. How to avoid the common errors: whole frame blurry, ghosting double images, smeared wheels.\n5. An A/B/C test: the same prompt with each blur level, and what to compare.\n \n### Output Format\nShort sections, then a phrase table: Level | Phrases | Best for.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. What vehicle are you animating?\n2. What feeling do you want?\n3. Which model?\nThen teach.",
