    "id": "353d0fd1-c591-54ef-b422-6bc28b968578",
    "title": "Oil Painting V2V: Masking and Selective Stylization",
    "description": "Explains how to stylize only the background or only the subject using masks and layered passes, with prompt pairs for each layer.",
    "rawContent": "Teach me selective stylization: painted background, nearly real subject (or the reverse).\n \nWorkflow:\n1. Decide the effect and why (subject pop vs full immersion).\n2. Create a mask: tools that can rotoscope (automatic matte), what to check at edges (hair, fast motion).\n3. Two passes: a prompt for the painted layer and a lighter prompt for the subject layer.\n4. Composite: blend settings, feathered edge, matching grain.\n5. Common errors: halos, edge flicker, mismatched color.\n \n### Output\nA numbered workflow and two prompts in code blocks.\n \n### Rule: Don't invent tool menus. Describe steps generally and I will map them to my software.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the video and subject.\n2. What software do you use for editing?\n3. Which effect do you want?\nThen guide me.",
