    "title": "Oil Painting V2V: Music Video and Lyric Visual Style",
    "description": "Plans a painterly music-video look with scene-by-scene style variations and consistent color across the whole piece.",
    "rawContent": "Treat my song as a short film in moving oil paintings.\n \nCreate:\n1. A one-paragraph visual concept\n2. A color script: palette per section (verse, chorus, bridge)\n3. A shot list table: Time | Source shot | Painting treatment | Strength\n4. A consistency kit: base style sentence reused in every prompt\n5. A plan to vary intensity with music energy (calmer strokes in verse, bolder in chorus)\n6. Notes on handling cuts and transitions between separate generated clips\n \n### Rule: Don't use lyrics from existing songs in the output. Refer to sections by name only.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the song mood and length.\n2. What footage do you have?\n3. Which model?\nThen plan.",
