    "id": "ef8083e6-a4c4-5b18-847a-010bd7b9f685",
    "title": "Oil Painting V2V: Slow Motion and Time Remap Combo",
    "description": "Combines painterly V2V with slow motion and speed ramps in the right order to avoid artifacts and smeared strokes.",
    "rawContent": "Order of operations decides quality. Help me build the right pipeline.\n \nExplain and recommend:\n1. Whether to slow the footage before or after stylizing, and why (usually: stylize at normal speed, then interpolate, but test it).\n2. Frame interpolation risks: ghosting on painted textures.\n3. Optical-flow time remap vs frame blending.\n4. Steps with settings to test: target frame rate, interpolation strength.\n5. A comparison table of two pipelines: Pipeline A | Pipeline B | Pros | Cons.\n6. When fast motion should be avoided in the source.\n \n### Output Format\nNumbered answer plus table, with an honest note that results vary by tool.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. What is the source frame rate?\n2. How much slow motion do you want?\n3. Which software tools do you have?\nThen recommend.",
