    "id": "283bad83-3817-592f-ab5b-b6aaa9c06f26",
    "title": "Anime V2V: Character Face Stylization Without Drift",
    "description": "Keeps faces recognizable and consistent while converting to anime features, with guidance on eyes, hair, and expressions.",
    "rawContent": "Convert faces to anime while keeping each person recognizable.\n \nSteps:\n1. Write a character sheet in words for each person: hair color and shape, eye color, face shape, clothing, key accessory.\n2. Insert the sheet into the prompt as the anchor, using the same wording every time.\n3. Choose the anime eye style: realistic proportions with simplified features, or larger stylized eyes. Explain the risk of each for expression accuracy.\n4. Keep expressions and lip movements from the source.\n5. Add negative phrases: face changing between frames, swapped hair color, extra lashes.\n \n### Output\nCharacter sheet template, final prompt under 130 words, negative prompt.\n \nConsent note: only stylize people who agreed.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the people in the clip.\n2. How big should the anime eyes be?\n3. Model?\nThen write.",
