    "id": "36915564-dbd2-5e6b-b058-b0270f28cb3e",
    "title": "Anime V2V: Cel-Shading and Color Banding Control",
    "description": "Defines flat color blocks, shadow shapes, and highlight style for a clean cel-shaded look that holds steady across frames.",
    "rawContent": "Describe how my anime shading should behave so it stays stable.\n \nDefine:\n1. Number of shading steps: base color plus one shadow tone (2-tone) or plus a highlight (3-tone)\n2. Shadow shape rules: hard-edged shapes following form, consistent light direction\n3. Highlight style: small sharp glints on hair and eyes\n4. Palette: limited set of colors with names (warm cream, sky blue, sage green)\n5. Banding and gradient: avoid smooth gradients except in the sky\n6. Words to include and exclude in the prompt\n \n### Output\nStyle spec table, then a prompt under 120 words, then the negative prompt (no gradients on skin, no glossy 3D shading).\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the scene and its lighting.\n2. Preferred tone: bright or moody?\n3. Model?\nThen write.",
