    "title": "Anime V2V: Action and Fast Motion Handling",
    "description": "Plans how to restyle fast action footage into anime without smearing, with prompt and clip-splitting strategies.",
    "rawContent": "Fast footage turns to mush in V2V. Design a plan that keeps action readable.\n \nProvide:\n1. What breaks first in fast motion (limbs, hair, background lines) and why.\n2. Prompt tricks: describe the motion as it is, and ask for bold simplified shapes with clean silhouettes.\n3. Source prep: shorter clips, higher frame rate, stable exposure.\n4. Strength settings: lower for fast moves, with the trade-offs.\n5. Optional anime tricks: speed lines added in post rather than generated.\n6. Clip splitting at moments of peak action and how to blend.\n \n### Output Format\nNumbered plan and a final prompt under 120 words.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the action in the clip.\n2. Frame rate of the source?\n3. Which model?\nThen plan.",
