    "title": "Anime V2V: Lip-Sync and Dialogue Scene Handling",
    "description": "Maintains mouth movement timing and clean anime-style mouths in dialogue footage, with fixes for drifting mouth shapes.",
    "rawContent": "Dialogue scenes need accurate mouth timing. Help me preserve it in an anime restyle.\n \nProcess:\n1. Prompt wording: \"mouth movements follow the original speech exactly\", simple clean mouth shapes, no teeth detail unless visible in the source.\n2. Choose how the anime style handles mouths: minimal (a few shapes) is more stable than detailed.\n3. Source prep: clear lighting on the face, a front or three-quarter angle, avoid fast head turns.\n4. Check method: play the output with the original audio and compare.\n5. Fix list: shorter clips, lower strength, mask the mouth region if supported, re-time in editing.\n \n### Output\nNumbered guidance, final prompt under 110 words, negative prompt (no mouth drift, no extra mouths, no frozen lips).\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the dialogue shot.\n2. Is audio available for checking?\n3. Model?\nThen continue.",
