    "id": "7702270d-adb6-54ed-9890-2f2e5b1b57b6",
    "title": "Anime V2V: Parameter Matrix and Seed Strategy",
    "description": "Builds a test matrix for style strength, consistency, seeds, and resolution to find the most stable anime look fast.",
    "rawContent": "Set up a systematic test so I find the best settings in few runs.\n \nProvide:\n1. Variables list: style strength, consistency or structure, seed, resolution, clip length.\n2. Round 1: vary style strength and consistency only, a 3x3 table with run IDs.\n3. Round 2: lock the best pair, test 4 seeds.\n4. Round 3: test resolution and length for the final.\n5. Scorecard: line stability, background stability, face match, motion match, 1-5 each.\n6. A stop rule: when a result is good enough.\n \n### Rule: Don't invent specific parameter names. Tell me to map to my tool.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Which video model or app?\n2. How many runs can you afford?\n3. What is your biggest problem?\nThen build the matrix.",
