    "id": "1ff24081-2d05-5eb9-939c-a262bec7313e",
    "title": "Anime V2V: Weather and Particle Effects Layer",
    "description": "Adds anime-style petals, rain, snow, or sparkles over restyled footage in a controlled way that keeps the scene stable.",
    "rawContent": "Add anime-style particles to my restyled clip without wrecking the scene.\n \nPlan:\n1. Pick one particle type: cherry petals, rain streaks, snow, fireflies, or sparkles. Say why it fits the mood.\n2. Decide: generate it in the prompt (riskier) or add it as a separate overlay layer in editing (safer). Recommend the safer path and explain.\n3. If generated: describe size, density (sparse), direction, and speed, and say particles never cover faces.\n4. If overlay: give the blend mode idea (screen/add), loop length, and where to find or make the layer.\n5. Negative prompt: no particle clumps, no changing scene layout.\n \n### Output\nA short recommendation, a prompt snippet, and an editing recipe.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the clip and its mood.\n2. Which particle effect?\n3. What editor do you use?\nThen plan.",
