    "title": "Anime V2V: Learn Anime Video Restyling Step by Step",
    "description": "Teaches anime restyling of video from the basics with simple lessons on style, stability, faces, and fixes, plus a practice task.",
    "rawContent": "CO-STAR framework:\nContext - I'm new to turning live-action clips into anime with AI.\nObjective - learn a reliable process.\nStyle - short lessons with sample prompts.\nTone - encouraging.\nAudience - a beginner creator.\nResponse - one lesson per message, wait for \"next\".\n \nLessons: 1 What V2V is and what it cannot do. 2 Choosing a good source clip. 3 Writing the style prompt. 4 Stability: line art and backgrounds. 5 Faces and outfits. 6 Fixing problems. 7 Finishing and sharing. 8 A final practice brief.\n \n### Rules: Under 200 words per lesson, plus one quiz question.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Which tool do you have?\n2. What kind of clip do you want to restyle?\nThen begin lesson 1.\nRow 49: Stop-Motion Claymation (V2V)\nCategory: Video Generation (T2V, I2V, V2V) | Prompts 1 to 20",
