    "id": "e7edf030-0d51-55c6-87a7-5908187138c0",
    "title": "Claymation V2V: Fingerprints and Clay Texture Realism",
    "description": "Adds believable thumbprints, tool marks, and seam lines so the clay feels sculpted by hand rather than digitally smoothed.",
    "rawContent": "Make the clay feel real. Give me a texture vocabulary for stop-motion V2V.\n \nProvide:\n1. 12 phrases for surface detail: thumbprints, smudged edges, tool marks, tiny air pits, lint specks, seams where clay pieces join\n2. Where each belongs (faces get gentle prints, clothes get rolled-texture strips)\n3. Material wording: matte, slightly waxy, soft highlights, no wet shine\n4. Three intensity levels: subtle, clear, heavy\n5. A warning: too much texture flickers; keep it consistent across frames\n \n### Output\nPhrase table with columns: Phrase | Where | Level. Then a combined prompt snippet under 50 words.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the main subject in your footage.\n2. Which intensity?\nThen write.",
