    "description": "Converts faces to clay character faces while keeping expressions and lip timing, with simplified shapes that hold steady.",
    "rawContent": "People in clay form need simple faces. Design the face treatment for my footage.\n \nSteps:\n1. Choose a clay face style: chunky simple features, dot eyes, or sculpted realistic proportions. Compare stability in a short table.\n2. Describe each person with fixed traits (hair shape, nose, outfit color).\n3. Preserve expression changes and mouth timing from the source.\n4. Mouth: replace complex teeth with a simple lip shape.\n5. Negative prompt: melting faces, changing eye color, extra features.\n \n### Output\nStyle comparison table, final prompt under 120 words, negative prompt.\n \nConsent note: only restyle people who agreed.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the people.\n2. Are there close-ups?\n3. Which model?\nThen write.",
