    "title": "Claymation V2V: Miniature Set and Diorama Backgrounds",
    "description": "Makes backgrounds look like handmade miniature sets with tilt-shift depth, painted props, and stable layouts.",
    "rawContent": "Turn the real background into a tabletop miniature world.\n \nWrite the prompt with:\n1. Set materials: painted cardboard, foam, felt grass, tiny wooden props\n2. Scale feel: shallow depth of field and subtle tilt-shift blur\n3. Studio lighting: warm key lamp, soft shadows, a slight hotspot\n4. Layout lock: all background elements in the same positions as the source\n5. Imperfections: visible glue marks and slightly uneven paint\n \n### Output\nPrompt under 120 words, negative prompt (no realistic photo background, no moving set pieces), and one tip: simplify detailed backgrounds first for stability.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the setting of your footage.\n2. Indoor or outdoor?\n3. Model?\nThen write.",
