    "id": "0954b3b0-74a9-551f-81ab-697be04ecb15",
    "title": "Claymation V2V: Motion Retiming to 12fps Workflow",
    "description": "Gives a precise editing workflow for converting smooth AI output to authentic 12fps stop-motion timing without ugly artifacts.",
    "rawContent": "Teach me the correct order for getting a real stop-motion rhythm.\n \nExplain:\n1. Why prompting for \"choppy\" often fails and editing works better\n2. Steps: render at normal frame rate, stylize, then drop frames (hold each frame for 2 at 24fps, called \"shooting on twos\")\n3. Optional \"ones\" on fast action, mixing rates for key moments\n4. Add subtle jitter or position wobble in the editor (2-3 pixels, random per frame)\n5. Boil effect: slight texture change every few frames, kept gentle\n6. Check list: no motion blur, no interpolation\n \n### Output Format\nNumbered steps with the generic names of effects. Don't invent menu paths.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Which editor do you use?\n2. What is your project frame rate?\nThen guide me.",
