    "title": "Claymation V2V: Crowd and Multi-Character Scenes",
    "description": "Plans multi-character clay scenes where each figure stays distinct, with stable counts, colors, and positions.",
    "rawContent": "More characters means more drift. Plan it carefully.\n \nProvide:\n1. A character roster table: Name | Clay color | Outfit | Signature trait | Position in frame\n2. A rule to keep the cast to 3 or 4 key figures; others become simple blobs or background shapes\n3. Prompt structure: scene sentence first, roster second, motion third\n4. Techniques: split into shorter clips, vary color per character, avoid overlaps\n5. Negative phrases: swapped outfits, merged figures, changing head counts\n6. Inspection checklist per 2 seconds\n \n### Output Format\nTable, final prompt under 140 words, negative prompt.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. How many people appear and what are they doing?\n2. Is the camera moving?\n3. Model?\nThen plan.",
