    "title": "Claymation V2V: Lighting Match for Mixed Media Compositing",
    "description": "Composites clay-styled characters onto real or painted backgrounds with matching light, shadow, and grain.",
    "rawContent": "Help me combine clay-styled subjects with a different background.\n \nExplain and plan:\n1. Light direction matching: analyze the background and describe the key light for the subject pass\n2. Shadow: create contact shadows under the subject, with soft edge falloff\n3. Grain and color: add the same grain and match black levels\n4. Edge cleanup for hair and fast movement\n5. Parallax or small camera shake shared by both layers\n6. Prompt for the subject pass on a plain background to make masking easier\n \n### Output\nWorkflow steps, subject-pass prompt, and a final inspection checklist.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the subject footage and the new background.\n2. What compositing tool do you use?\nThen plan.",
