    "rawContent": "Add variety to my clay look with other handmade materials.\n \nPlease design:\n1. A material map: clay for characters, felt for clothing and grass, paper cutouts for far backgrounds, wire for thin props and antennae\n2. Prompt wording for each material's texture and edge quality\n3. Depth layering: paper cutouts at the back, felt mid, clay front, with small gaps and shadows\n4. Rule: no more than 3 materials per shot to keep stability\n5. Negative phrases: glossy plastic, photographic textures, digital gradients\n \n### Output\nMaterial table: Element | Material | Wording. Then a prompt of under 120 words and a negative prompt.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe your scene and characters.\n2. Which materials appeal to you?\n3. Model?\nThen write.",
