    "id": "6c980bac-9baf-58cf-abca-8ff12f173e4c",
    "title": "Corporate Avatar: Multilingual Localization Plan",
    "description": "Plans how to produce the same presenter video in several languages with consistent look, accurate translation, and natural lip-sync.",
    "rawContent": "Plan a multilingual version of my presenter video.\n \nCover:\n1. Script adaptation: translate meaning, not words; idioms, units, dates, and cultural references\n2. Length differences between languages and how to keep timing\n3. Native review step before generation\n4. Lip-sync notes: tools handle languages differently; test each\n5. Consistent avatar look across versions\n6. Subtitles vs dubbing decision table\n7. Folder and naming convention\n \n### Output\nWorkflow steps, a table: Language | Script status | Review | Lip-sync test | Final.\n \n### Rule: Recommend native speaker review for every language.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Source language and target languages?\n2. What kind of content?\n3. Which avatar tool?\nThen plan.",
