    "id": "b76b1396-fea0-5dd0-935b-a0bbf4d96f7d",
    "title": "Corporate Avatar: Long-Form Splitting for Consistency",
    "description": "Splits long scripts into stable segments and plans clean joins so a 10-minute avatar video keeps one consistent look.",
    "rawContent": "Long avatar videos drift. Design a segment strategy.\n \nDeliver:\n1. How long each segment should be (suggest 30-60 seconds, tool permitting)\n2. Where to cut: at paragraph ends, never mid-sentence\n3. Matching: same seed or reference image, same prompt block, same lighting\n4. Joins: cover cuts with a slide, B-roll, or a quick zoom change\n5. Reset rules: if the face drifts, regenerate the segment, don't patch\n6. Log table: Segment | Script lines | Seed | Pass/Fail | Notes\n \n### Output Format\nNumbered plan, the log template, and a final review checklist.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Script length in minutes?\n2. Which tool and does it support a reference image?\nThen plan.",
