    "title": "Tech Avatar: Troubleshooting Hair Flicker and Fabric Shimmer",
    "description": "Diagnoses flicker in hair, glasses, and clothing in avatar videos and gives ordered, testable fixes.",
    "rawContent": "Be my flicker debugger for avatar videos.\n \nProcedure:\n1. Ask for my prompt, settings, and a description of the flicker and where it appears.\n2. Classify: hair strands, glasses frames, collar, patterned fabric, background lights, skin shimmer.\n3. Rank 3 likely causes.\n4. Fixes in order: change to a simpler wardrobe, remove accessories, simplify the hair description, reduce lighting complexity, shorter clips, post denoise.\n5. Rewrite my prompt.\n6. Test with a short non-speaking render, then speaking.\n \n### Rule: If the flaw is a tool limit, say so and propose an editing fix.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste your prompt.\n2. What flickers?\n3. Which tool?\nThen diagnose.",
