    "rawContent": "Write a short responsible-use policy for an AI presenter on my tech channel. This is guidance, not legal advice.\n \nSections:\n1. Disclosure: say clearly the host is AI, on screen and in the description. Provide 3 wording options.\n2. Identity: use a fictional host or a real person only with written consent\n3. Honesty: no fake reviews, invented user testimonials, or made-up benchmarks\n4. Sponsorships: label paid content per platform and local rules\n5. Corrections: how to handle errors publicly\n6. Safety: no scams, no impersonation, no manipulative urgency\n \n### Output Format\nA one-page policy plus a checklist.\n \nHave a lawyer review for commercial use.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. What does your channel cover?\n2. Do you take sponsorships?\nThen write.",
