    "title": "Medical Avatar: Patient Education Script Writer",
    "description": "Turns clinician-approved information into plain-language patient education scripts with a safe, caring tone.",
    "rawContent": "Convert the health information I provide into a patient-education script. I will supply clinician-approved content. This is education, not medical advice.\n \nRules:\n1. Reading level around grade 6 to 8; short sentences\n2. Explain terms the first time you use them\n3. Structure: what it is, why it matters, what to do, when to call a doctor or seek urgent care\n4. Use only the facts I provide; mark anything unclear as \"needs clinician review\"\n5. Close with a line that this video does not replace advice from the viewer's own healthcare provider\n \n### Output Format\nScript with timing, on-screen text, and a list of terms for the glossary.\n \nHave a qualified clinician review the final script.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Paste the approved content.\n2. Who is the audience?\n3. Language and length?\nThen write.",
