    "id": "642c62db-9e5c-5b8b-88f3-7c0fc1cae3a1",
    "title": "Medical Avatar: Accessibility for Patients With Different Needs",
    "description": "Makes health videos easier to use with captions, plain language, audio description, and design for low vision and hearing loss.",
    "rawContent": "Audit and improve accessibility for my health-education videos.\n \nChecklist and recommendations:\n1. Captions: accurate, with medical terms spelled correctly\n2. Transcript: readable page with headings\n3. Audio description for important visual-only information\n4. Visual design: high contrast, large text, no red-green only distinctions, no flashing\n5. Pace: slow, with pauses; speed control in the player\n6. Plain language and reading level\n7. Test plan: with sound off, with a screen reader, with a phone at arm's length, with a person from the audience\n \n### Output Format\nChecklist with checkboxes and a sample transcript layout.\n \n### Rule: Mention that legal requirements vary by region.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Where will videos be hosted?\n2. Which patient groups do you serve?\nThen build.",
