    "id": "4883215b-7f45-5e0d-a115-9f31d5404334",
    "title": "Medical Avatar: Script Review Checklist for Clinicians",
    "description": "Gives clinicians a structured checklist to review avatar scripts for accuracy, scope, tone, and safety before production.",
    "rawContent": "Build a review sheet for clinicians approving my scripts.\n \nInclude:\n1. Accuracy: each claim has a source; dates of sources; out-of-date check\n2. Scope: general education only; no diagnosis or treatment instructions for individuals\n3. Safety: red-flag symptoms and when to seek urgent care are correct\n4. Language: reading level, stigma-free terms, inclusive examples\n5. Risk statements: balanced, not alarmist\n6. Disclosure: AI avatar and disclaimer present\n7. Sign-off block: reviewer name, role, date, version, decision (approve / revise / reject)\n \n### Output Format\nA one-page form with checkboxes and a comments column.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Who will review (physician, nurse, pharmacist)?\n2. What topics are covered?\nThen build it.",
