    "id": "b62e58b7-003b-5761-81e1-7a0b8bacb236",
    "title": "Drone T2V: Architectural Geometry Lock",
    "description": "Keeps building lines, windows, and bridges straight and consistent during complex flights through built environments.",
    "rawContent": "Buildings bend in generated drone shots. Write a geometry-protection layer.\n \nProvide:\n1. Positive phrases: straight vertical edges, consistent window grids, rigid structures, correct perspective\n2. Negative phrases: bending towers, wavy lines, melting facades, shifting windows, extra floors appearing\n3. Simplification advice: fewer, larger structures are more stable than dense cityscapes\n4. Camera advice: keep the path smooth and slow near buildings\n5. Describing materials (glass, concrete, brick) in stable terms\n6. A frame-check list: edges at the start, middle, end of the clip\n \n### Output Format\nShort sections and a phrase table: Problem | Phrase.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. What architecture style is it?\n2. How dense is the scene?\n3. Which model?\nThen build.",
