    "title": "Drone T2V: Landscape Texture Consistency",
    "description": "Maintains stable forests, rock, water, and field textures so terrain doesn't crawl or boil during aerial motion.",
    "rawContent": "Terrain textures crawl in aerial clips. Help me stabilize them.\n \nWrite:\n1. Texture descriptions that are readable from altitude: patchwork fields, evergreen canopy, layered rock faces, calm lake surface\n2. Scale words that keep detail stable: broad, large-scale, simple patterns\n3. Weather and light that reduce flicker: even overcast or soft low sun\n4. Words to avoid: hyper-detailed, intricate, sparkling, every leaf\n5. Negative phrases: crawling textures, shimmering water, flickering trees\n \n### Output\nPhrase table (Use | Avoid), then a prompt snippet under 60 words.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. What landscape?\n2. Altitude of the shot?\n3. Model?\nThen write.",
