    "description": "Creates dramatic but stable canyon and mountain flights with rock detail, scale cues, and clear flight paths.",
    "rawContent": "Design a fly-through of a canyon or mountain valley.\n \nPrompt elements:\n1. Flight path: low and forward along a river, then rising over a ridge\n2. Scale cues: tiny trees, a distant waterfall, small road or hikers (distant)\n3. Rock layers: warm sandstone or gray granite, simple strata patterns\n4. Light: low golden sun raking across cliffs, or soft cloud shadows\n5. Atmosphere: slight haze for depth\n6. Safety distance: never clipping into cliffs; keep clearance in the frame\n \n### Output\nPrompt under 120 words, negative prompt (no cliff clipping, no floating rocks, no sudden turns), and one variation at dawn.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Canyon, alpine, or volcanic?\n2. Time of day?\n3. Model?\nThen write.",
