    "description": "Plans a smooth descent through forest canopy to a clearing with stable foliage and soft shafts of light.",
    "rawContent": "Describe a drone shot that descends through a forest canopy.\n \nStages:\nStage 1 - Start high above the canopy: a green carpet of treetops, mist in gaps.\nStage 2 - Slow descent through a gap between trees.\nStage 3 - Pass trunks at a safe distance, with light shafts and drifting spores.\nStage 4 - Level out above a stream or clearing.\n \n### Rules:\n- Foliage is broad shapes and stays steady.\n- No branches intersecting with the camera.\n \n### Output\nPrompt under 130 words, negative prompt (no clipping branches, no flickering leaves, no animals unless asked), and a tip to split into two clips if the model struggles.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Forest type (pine, tropical, autumn)?\n2. Time of day?\n3. Model?\nThen write.",
