    "description": "Explains how to describe speed, altitude, and gimbal smoothness so the shot feels like a real drone, not a shaky camera.",
    "rawContent": "Teach me to control the feel of a drone shot with words.\n \nProvide:\n1. Altitude bands: low (3-10 m), medium (30-60 m), high (100 m+) and what each reveals\n2. Speed words: crawling, gliding, cruising, fast sweep, and which look cinematic\n3. Smoothness: \"gimbal-stabilized\", \"no shake\", \"constant velocity\"\n4. Lens feel: wide, standard, with horizon level\n5. A table: Goal | Altitude | Speed | Phrase\n6. Common mistakes: too many motions, conflicting speed words, shake terms\n \n### Output Format\nShort sections and the table.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. What feeling do you want (serene, thrilling, epic)?\n2. Which scene?\nThen write.",
