    "description": "Plans how to chain several short clips into one long continuous flight with matching light, direction, and position.",
    "rawContent": "Long continuous flights need clip chaining. Design the plan.\n \nProvide:\n1. Break the flight into 3 to 5 segments, each with start and end positions\n2. Continuity sheet: time of day, light direction, weather, speed, altitude, heading\n3. Overlap: the last frame of clip A as the first frame of clip B if the tool supports image-to-video\n4. Prompt template reused across segments, with only the path part changed\n5. Join methods: match cuts on motion, cross-dissolve, whip pan\n6. Log table: Segment | Prompt | Seed | Result | Fix\n \n### Output Format\nPlan and templates.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the full journey.\n2. Does your tool support image-to-video continuation?\nThen plan.",
