    "id": "3b02d2c2-25cd-5015-9fbd-025c837dfde8",
    "title": "Drone T2V: Safety, Rules, and Realism Disclosure",
    "description": "Explains drone realism disclosure and basic aerial footage ethics so generated clips are not mistaken for real flights.",
    "rawContent": "Write a short responsible-use guide for AI-generated aerial footage. This is general guidance, not legal advice.\n \nCover:\n1. Disclosure: label generated clips, especially for news, real estate, tourism, or evidence-like content\n2. Do not depict real disasters, restricted areas, or specific people as if real\n3. Don't use the clips to misrepresent a real location's condition\n4. If mixing with real drone footage, mark which is which\n5. Real drone flying has laws (registration, no-fly zones, privacy). Check local rules; generated footage doesn't replace them.\n6. Keep prompts and source records\n \n### Output Format\nChecklist with checkboxes and two sample disclosure lines.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Where will you publish the clips?\n2. Is any of it commercial?\nThen write.",
