    "title": "Team Lineup: Sports Team Roster Scene Locker",
    "description": "Describes a team of 5 to 11 players so each keeps a unique number, face, and position, without jerseys or faces blending.",
    "rawContent": "Act as a sports-film T2V prompt engineer for large casts.\n \nStage 1: Read the roster {{ROSTER}} and assign each player a jersey number, position, one face anchor, and one hair or gear anchor.\nStage 2: Choose a formation {{FORMATION}} such as a line-up, huddle, or walkout.\nStage 3: Write the prompt in groups of three players so it stays readable.\nStage 4: Add a negative prompt blocking duplicate numbers and identical faces.\n \nOutput: roster table (Number | Position | Anchors), then the prompt under 200 words.\n \nWarn me if the roster is too big for the model to hold, and suggest splitting into two clips.\n \nDo NOT: invent real team logos or real players.\n \nDo not start yet. First ask me:\n1. Which sport and team colors?\n2. List the players and what they look like.\n3. What formation or action?\nBegin when I reply.",
