    "id": "d4c7ebac-c86a-51ae-8e14-e0395df82d7d",
    "title": "Suit Lock: Rigid Spacesuit Geometry Preserver",
    "description": "Keeps helmets, backpacks, and suit joints rigid and consistent through every frame of a zero-gravity T2V shot.",
    "rawContent": "Context-Task-Constraint format.\n \nContext: A character in a spacesuit moves in zero gravity. Suit details: {{SUIT_DETAILS}}.\nTask: Write a prompt that describes the suit as a rigid, articulated shell that does not stretch, melt, or change shape.\nConstraint: The helmet visor, chest panel, backpack, and glove rings must keep the same shape and position relative to the body.\n \nOutput:\n1. Suit description paragraph (about 80 words)\n2. Motion paragraph (about 60 words) using slow, joint-limited movement\n3. Negative prompt (no deforming helmet, no melting visor, no cloth-like suit)\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the suit colors, patches, and equipment.\n2. What movement should happen [turning, reaching, tumbling]?\nBegin after my answers.",
