    "description": "Describes how flames and gas look in microgravity, as round, blue, and slow instead of tall, orange, and upward.",
    "rawContent": "Write a science-accurate prompt about fire in zero gravity.\n \nKey facts to apply:\n- Flames form small spheres or domes, not tall teardrops\n- They burn blue and dim, with slow motion\n- Smoke does not rise, it spreads slowly in all directions\n \nSubject: {{FIRE_SOURCE}} in {{LOCATION}}.\n \nOutput:\n1. Prompt under 130 words\n2. Negative prompt (no rising flames, no orange tall fire, no smoke going up)\n3. One safety note: this is a visual depiction only, never a how-to for fire experiments.\n \nVerify science details if you are publishing educational content.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. What is burning, such as a candle or a small spark?\n2. Where is it happening?\n3. Is the tone educational or dramatic?\nBegin after I answer.",
