    "title": "Glasses and Hair: Occlusion Handling for Face Replacement",
    "description": "Handles glasses, hats, hair strands, hands, and microphones passing over a face so the swap stays clean at the overlap.",
    "rawContent": "Create a prompt strategy for faces that are partly covered in a video.\n \nOccluders: {{OCCLUDER_LIST}}\n \nFor each occluder, write:\n- Layer order (face is behind it or in front)\n- A rule for the edge (clean, no blur, no transparent leak)\n- A note on reflection or shadow it casts on the new face\n \nThen provide:\n1. A combined prompt (under 150 words)\n2. A fallback tip, such as masking those frames manually\n \n### Do NOT: tell the model to remove the occluder unless I ask.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Please ask me:\n1. What passes in front of the face [glasses, hair, hands]?\n2. How often and for how long?\n3. Which tool do you use?\nBegin after you receive my answers.",
