    "id": "8ec3027e-065b-56e1-aac6-fac9dbee517e",
    "title": "Stylized Swap: Face Replacement for Animation or Illustration",
    "description": "Handles swapping a real face into a stylized, painted, or cartoon video look while keeping the original art style consistent.",
    "rawContent": "Using CO-STAR:\n- Context: my video has an art style of {{ART_STYLE}} and I want to place the identity {{IDENTITY}} into it\n- Objective: the face must look native to the style, not pasted on\n- Style: match line weight, shading, and color palette of the original\n- Tone: consistent\n- Audience: V2V model\n- Response: prompt plus negative prompt\n \nCover how to handle eyes, outlines, and shadows in that style, and what level of realism to keep from the new identity (high, medium, low).\n \nOutput: prompt under 140 words, negative prompt (no photorealistic face on flat art), and a level recommendation.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. What art style is the video?\n2. Which identity features must remain recognizable?\n3. How realistic should the face look?\nBegin after you answer.",
