    "title": "Street Glow: Artificial Light Source Addition Planner",
    "description": "Plans where to add lamps, neon, headlights, and window glow in a night conversion, with believable color and falloff.",
    "rawContent": "Task: Plan the artificial lights for a daytime video being converted to night.\n \nScene details: {{SCENE_DETAILS}}.\n \nStages:\n1. List every place a light could logically exist (poles, windows, signs, vehicles).\n2. Pick 4 to 6 sources and give each a color temperature (warm yellow, cool white, neon pink).\n3. Describe the light falloff and the pool of light on the ground.\n4. Write one prompt that adds only these lights.\n \nOutput: light table (Source | Color | Radius), then the prompt under 140 words.\n \nDo NOT: add lights where no fixture could exist.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. What is in the scene [street, room, park]?\n2. What mood or color palette do you prefer?\n3. Is the camera moving?\nBegin after your replies.",
