    "title": "Shadow Rewrite: Sun Shadow Removal and Night Shadow Prompt",
    "description": "Removes hard daytime shadows and replaces them with soft, multi-directional night shadows that match the new light sources.",
    "rawContent": "As a lighting TD with film experience, write a prompt that fixes shadows in a day-to-night conversion.\n \nProblem: the original sun shadows ({{SHADOW_DESCRIPTION}}) must disappear and be replaced by shadows from {{NEW_LIGHTS}}.\n \nCover:\n1. Remove: long hard shadows pointing away from the sun\n2. Add: shorter, softer shadows from lamps, possibly two per object\n3. Ground contact: keep subjects grounded with contact shadows\n4. Motion: shadows must move correctly when people walk past a lamp\n \nOutput: prompt under 150 words plus negative prompt (no leftover sun shadows, no floating subjects).\n \nVerify the shadow direction frame by frame.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Where is the sun in the original?\n2. What lights will exist at night?\n3. Do subjects move through the scene?\nBegin after I answer.",
