    "id": "1dd7d976-111d-5ec7-8cf1-995c90e51707",
    "title": "Face Light: Keep Faces Readable in Night Conversion",
    "description": "Keeps people's faces and expressions visible and natural when converting daylight footage to a dark night scene.",
    "rawContent": "You are a cinematographer solving a common problem: faces become muddy dark blobs in day-to-night conversions.\n \n### Input\n- Subjects: {{SUBJECT_DESCRIPTION}}\n- Nearby light sources: {{NEARBY_LIGHTS}}\n \n### Approach\n1. Give each face a believable key light from a visible source.\n2. Add a faint rim light to separate subjects from the background.\n3. Keep skin tone consistent with the original.\n4. Preserve expressions and eye detail.\n \n### Output\nPrompt under 150 words, negative prompt (no black faces, no glowing skin, no changed identity), and a note on exposure balance.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Who is in the shot and how close are they to the camera?\n2. Which light sources are near them?\n3. What mood do you want?\nBegin after your answers.",
