    "title": "Moon Logic: Moonlight Direction and Phase Consistency Prompt",
    "description": "Sets one consistent moonlight direction and brightness so shadows, rim lights, and reflections agree across the whole scene.",
    "rawContent": "Write a moonlight consistency guide plus a prompt for a night-converted clip.\n \nInputs: scene layout {{SCENE_LAYOUT}}, camera facing {{CAMERA_DIRECTION}}, moon phase {{MOON_PHASE}}.\n \nDecide:\n1. Where the moon sits in the sky or whether it is hidden\n2. Which side of objects receive cool rim light\n3. How long and soft the shadows are\n4. How water or glass reflects it\n \nOutput: a diagram-style text list (Left, Center, Right) and a prompt under 120 words.\n \nDo NOT: let two moons or two light directions appear.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Which way is the camera pointing?\n2. What phase of moon should it be?\n3. What is in the scene?\nBegin after my answers.",
