    "title": "Scratch Lab: Film Scratch, Dust, and Hair Overlay Designer",
    "description": "Designs the pattern, density, and animation of film scratches, dust specks, and gate hairs for an authentic 1920s look.",
    "rawContent": "Task: Plan realistic film damage for a 1920s restyle.\n \nCover each type:\n1. Vertical scratches (thin, bright, flickering, short life)\n2. Dust and dirt specks (random, dark and light, fast)\n3. Hairs and fibers near the frame edge\n4. Emulsion blotches\n5. Reel-change cue marks, optional\n \nFor each: density (low, medium, high), size, how it moves, and how long it stays.\n \nThen write a prompt using {{DAMAGE_LEVEL}} damage that does not hide faces.\n \nOutput: damage table, prompt under 140 words, negative prompt (no scratches over key subjects for long).\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. What damage level [clean restoration, worn, badly damaged]?\n2. Is there a main subject whose face must stay clear?\nBegin after I answer.",
