    "title": "Grain Dial: Film Grain and Contrast Curve Prompt Writer",
    "description": "Specifies grain size, contrast, and tonal range typical of 1920s orthochromatic film so the black-and-white look feels period-accurate.",
    "rawContent": "As a film historian and colorist, write a V2V prompt that recreates 1920s tonal qualities.\n \nCover these elements:\n1. Orthochromatic response: reds appear dark, blues appear bright\n2. High contrast with crushed blacks and bright highlights\n3. Soft focus and slight halation around lights\n4. Coarse, moving grain\n5. Slight vignetting\n \nApply to: {{SCENE_DESCRIPTION}}.\n \nOutput: a prompt under 150 words, negative prompt (no modern HDR, no clean digital noise), and a short note on how each element affects the final look.\n \nVerify historical claims if you are using this for education.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. What is in the scene?\n2. Are there strongly red or blue objects?\n3. How authentic or stylized should it be?\nBegin after my answers.",
