    "title": "Face Seal: Facial Feature Locking Prompt Builder",
    "description": "Builds a compact facial identity block that holds eye shape, nose, jawline, and skin marks stable through speech and motion.",
    "rawContent": "Using CO-STAR:\n- Context: character face from a reference sheet, {{FACE_DETAILS}}\n- Objective: keep identity stable while the head turns, talks, and emotes\n- Style: {{REALISM_LEVEL}}\n- Tone: neutral technical\n- Audience: T2V model\n- Response: a face lock block of 40 to 60 words plus negative prompt\n \nInclude: face shape, eyes (shape, color, spacing), brows, nose, lips, jaw, skin marks, and age cues.\n \nAdd a \"stability sentence\": the face stays the same during turns, smiles, and speech.\n \nNegative prompt: no face morph, no age change, no feature drift, no extra marks.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the face on your sheet.\n2. Does the character talk or show strong emotions?\n3. Is the style realistic, stylized, or 3D?\nBegin after I answer.",
