    "description": "Turns a character's colors into named and coded palette lines so skin, hair, and clothing colors stay exactly consistent across clips.",
    "rawContent": "Create a color lock for my character.\n \nInput colors: {{COLOR_LIST}} (hex codes if known).\n \nSteps:\n1. Name each color in plain words a video model understands (for example \"deep teal\", \"warm sand beige\").\n2. Pair each name with its hex code.\n3. Assign each color to a body part or garment.\n4. Add lighting caution: colors may shift under warm or cool light, so write a sentence that keeps hue stable.\n \nOutput: palette table (Part | Color name | Hex) and a prompt sentence under 60 words.\n \nWarn me that video models treat hex codes loosely, so use words as the main anchor.\n \nDo not start the task yet. Ask me:\n1. What colors does the character use?\n2. Do you have hex codes?\n3. What lighting is in the scene?\nBegin after I answer.",
