    "title": "Hair Physics: Locked Hairstyle in Motion Prompt",
    "description": "Keeps hairstyle shape, color, and parting stable while allowing believable motion in wind, running, or turning.",
    "rawContent": "Write a prompt for hair that moves naturally but never changes style.\n \nHair: {{HAIR_DESCRIPTION}}\nMotion: {{MOTION_TYPE}} [wind, running, head turn, rain]\n \nRules:\n1. The length, color, and parting stay the same.\n2. Movement is described as strands lifting and settling, not changing shape.\n3. Ties, clips, and braids remain intact.\n4. Wet or windy states must not darken or lighten the hair color.\n \nOutput: prompt under 110 words and negative prompt (no changing hair length, no new hair color, no hairstyle swap).\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. Describe the hairstyle and color.\n2. What motion or weather affects it?\nBegin after I answer.",
