    "title": "Animation Ready: Clay Scene Layer Separation for Motion",
    "description": "Plans how to separate a clay scene into layers so a motion designer can animate each part later.",
    "rawContent": "Act as a motion design producer.\n \nScene idea: {{SCENE_IDEA}}\n \nPlan the image prompts so the scene can be animated:\n1. Break into layers: background, floor, large objects, small props, characters, effects\n2. Write a separate prompt for each layer on a plain flat color background\n3. Keep the same style prefix and lighting for all layers\n4. Add notes on which layer should move and how\n5. Recommend export format and naming\n \nOutput: layer table and prompts under 60 words each.\n \nWarn me that AI rarely produces perfectly separated layers, so plan for manual cleanup.\n \nDo not start yet. Ask me:\n1. What is the scene?\n2. What should move?\n3. Which animation tool will you use?\nBegin after I respond.",
